1
00:00:00,129 --> 00:00:03,870
There is no audience here tonight in this hall at the National Constitution Center.
今晚在国家宪法中心的这个大厅里没有观众。

2
00:00:03,910 --> 00:00:07,251
This is an intimate setting for two candidates who have never met.
这是一个适合两位从未见过面的候选人的亲密环境。

3
00:00:07,551 --> 00:00:09,311
President Trump won the coin toss.
特朗普总统赢得了抛硬币的机会。

4
00:00:09,331 --> 00:00:12,052
He chose to deliver the final closing statement of the evening.
他选择在今晚发表最后的总结发言。

5
00:00:12,372 --> 00:00:14,713
Vice President Harris selected the podium to the right.
哈里斯副总统选择了右侧的讲台。

6
00:00:15,053 --> 00:00:17,093
So let's now welcome the candidates to the stage.
现在让我们欢迎候选人上台。

7
00:00:17,173 --> 00:00:20,094
Vice President Kamala Harris and President Donald Trump.
哈里斯副总统和特朗普总统。

8
00:00:27,798 --> 00:00:29,909
Kamala Harris, let's have a good debate.
卡马拉·哈里斯，愿我们有一场良好的辩论。

9
00:00:29,929 --> 00:00:30,251
Thank you.
谢谢。

10
00:00:32,702 --> 00:00:33,483
Welcome to you both.
欢迎你们两位。

11
00:00:33,623 --> 00:00:34,503
It's wonderful to have you.
很高兴你们能来到这里。

12
00:00:34,543 --> 00:00:35,964
It's an honor to have you both here tonight.
今晚能有你们在这里真是荣幸。

13
00:00:36,204 --> 00:00:36,825
Good evening.
晚上好。

14
00:00:36,905 --> 00:00:39,807
We are looking forward to a spirited and thoughtful debate.
我们期待一场充满活力和深思的辩论。

15
00:00:40,247 --> 00:00:41,028
So let's get started.
那么，让我们开始吧。

16
00:00:41,488 --> 00:00:48,353
I want to begin tonight with the issue that voters repeatedly say is their number one issue, and that is the economy and the cost of living in this country.
我想今晚从选民们反复表示的首要问题开始，那就是这个国家的经济和生活成本。

17
00:00:48,853 --> 00:00:58,119
Vice President Harris, you and President Trump were elected four years ago, and your opponent on the stage here tonight often asks his supporters, are you better off than you were four years ago?
哈里斯副总统，您和特朗普总统四年前当选，而今晚在这里的对手经常问他的支持者，你们比四年前过得更好吗？

18
00:00:58,619 --> 00:01:02,542
When it comes to the economy, do you believe Americans are better off than they were four years ago?
在经济方面，您认为美国人比四年前过得更好吗？

19
00:01:03,603 --> 00:01:14,576
So, I was raised as a middle class kid, and I am actually the only person on this stage who has a plan that is about lifting up the middle class and working people of America.
我是在中产阶级家庭长大的，实际上我是这个舞台上唯一有计划提升中产阶级和美国工人的人。

20
00:01:15,357 --> 00:01:20,042
I believe in the ambition, the aspirations, the dreams of the American people.
我相信美国人民的雄心、愿望和梦想。

21
00:01:20,603 --> 00:01:26,048
And that is why I imagine and have actually a plan to build what I call an opportunity economy.
这就是为什么我设想并实际上有一个计划来建立我所称的机会经济。

22
00:01:26,068 --> 00:01:27,269
Because here's the thing.
因为事情是这样的。

23
00:01:27,810 --> 00:01:31,373
We know that we have a shortage of homes and housing.
我们知道我们面临住房短缺的问题。

24
00:01:31,873 --> 00:01:34,696
And the cost of housing is too expensive for far too many people.
而且住房成本对太多人来说过于昂贵。

25
00:01:35,336 --> 00:01:37,738
We know that young families need support.
我们知道年轻家庭需要支持。

26
00:01:38,579 --> 00:01:55,081
to raise their children, and I intend on extending a tax cut for those families of $6,000, which is the largest child tax credit that we have given in a long time, so that those young families can afford to buy a crib, buy a car seat, buy clothes for their children.
以抚养孩子，我打算为这些家庭提供6000美元的减税，这是我们很久以来给予的最大儿童税收抵免，这样这些年轻家庭就能负担得起婴儿床、儿童座椅和孩子的衣服。

27
00:01:55,942 --> 00:01:59,425
My passion, one of them, is small businesses.
我热爱的一件事就是小企业。

28
00:01:59,645 --> 00:02:04,369
I was actually – my mother raised my sister and me, but there was a woman who helped raise us.
实际上，我的母亲抚养了我和我的姐姐，但还有一位女性帮助抚养我们。

29
00:02:04,449 --> 00:02:05,810
We call her our second mother.
我们称她为我们的第二位母亲。

30
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:07,091
She was a small business owner.
她是一位小企业主。

31
00:02:07,251 --> 00:02:08,652
I love our small businesses.
我热爱我们的小企业。

32
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:18,340
My plan is to give a $50,000 tax deduction to startup small businesses, knowing they are part of the backbone of America's economy.
我的计划是给初创小企业提供5万美元的税收扣除，因为我知道它们是美国经济的支柱。

33
00:02:19,061 --> 00:02:22,763
My opponent, on the other hand, his plan is to do what he has done before.
而我的对手，他的计划是继续他以前的做法。

34
00:02:23,584 --> 00:02:31,614
which is to provide a tax cut for billionaires and big corporations, which will result in $5 trillion to America's deficit.
也就是为亿万富翁和大企业提供减税，这将导致美国的赤字增加5万亿美元。

35
00:02:32,075 --> 00:02:41,807
My opponent has a plan that I call the Trump sales tax, which would be a 20% tax on everyday goods that you rely on to get through the month.
我的对手有一个我称之为特朗普销售税的计划，这将对你依赖的日常商品征收20%的税。

36
00:02:42,748 --> 00:03:01,540
Economists have said that that Trump sales tax would actually result for middle-class families in about $4,000 more a year because of his policies and his ideas about what should be the backs of middle-class people paying for tax cuts for billionaires.
经济学家表示，这项特朗普销售税实际上会使中产阶级家庭每年多花约4000美元，因为他的政策和关于中产阶级需要为亿万富翁的减税买单的想法。

37
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:02,933
President Trump.
特朗普总统。

38
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:20,172
Tariff will be substantial in some cases.
关税在某些情况下将是相当可观的。

39
00:03:20,252 --> 00:03:39,550
I took in billions and billions of dollars as you know from China In fact, they never took the tariff off because it was so much money They can't it would totally destroy everything that they've set out to do They're taking in billions of dollars from China and other places They've left the tariffs on when I had it I had tariffs and yet I had no inflation look, we've had a
众所周知，我从中国获得了数十亿美元，实际上，他们从未取消关税，因为这笔钱太多了，他们不能取消，这将完全摧毁他们设定的所有目标。

40
00:03:40,291 --> 00:03:44,432
Terrible economy because inflation has which is really known as a country buster.
他们从中国和其他地方获得数十亿美元。

41
00:03:44,452 --> 00:04:08,839
It breaks up countries We have inflation like very few people have ever seen before probably the worst in our nation's history We were at 21 percent But that's being generous because many things are 50 60 70 and 80 percent higher than they were just a few years ago This has been a disaster for people for the middle class but for every class on top of that we have millions of people pouring into our country from
当我实施关税时，我没有通货膨胀，看看我们经历的

42
00:04:09,399 --> 00:04:13,323
prisons and jails from mental institutions and insane asylums.
可怕的经济，因为通货膨胀，实际上被称为国家破坏者。

43
00:04:13,784 --> 00:04:21,851
And they're coming in and they're taking jobs that are occupied right now by African Americans and Hispanics and also unions.
它会撕裂国家。我们经历的通货膨胀是极少数人从未见过的，可能是我们国家历史上最糟糕的。

44
00:04:21,972 --> 00:04:23,613
Unions are going to be affected very soon.
我们曾达到21%，但这已经算是宽容，因为许多东西比几年前高出50%、60%、70%和80%。

45
00:04:24,034 --> 00:04:25,075
And you see what's happening.
这对中产阶级以及各个阶层的人都是一场灾难，此外，我们还有数以百万计的人从

46
00:04:25,095 --> 00:04:27,817
You see what's happening with towns throughout the United States.
监狱、精神病院和疯人院涌入我们的国家。

47
00:04:27,857 --> 00:04:29,799
You look at Springfield, Ohio.
他们进来后，正在占据现在由非裔美国人和西班牙裔以及工会占据的工作。

48
00:04:30,079 --> 00:04:32,362
You look at Aurora in Colorado.
工会将很快受到影响。

49
00:04:32,862 --> 00:04:34,383
They are taking over the towns.
你看到发生了什么。

50
00:04:34,423 --> 00:04:35,744
They're taking over buildings.
你看看美国各地城镇发生了什么。

51
00:04:35,784 --> 00:04:37,125
They're going in violently.
你看看俄亥俄州的斯普林菲尔德。

52
00:04:37,506 --> 00:04:44,010
These are the people that she and Biden let into our country, and they're destroying our country.
你看看科罗拉多州的奥罗拉。他们正在占领这些城镇。

53
00:04:44,331 --> 00:04:45,271
They're dangerous.
他们很危险。

54
00:04:45,572 --> 00:04:49,294
They're at the highest level of criminality, and we have to get them out.
他们的犯罪水平达到了历史最高点，我们必须把他们清除。

55
00:04:49,354 --> 00:04:50,495
We have to get them out fast.
我们必须迅速把他们清除。

56
00:04:50,896 --> 00:04:54,638
I created one of the greatest economies in the history of our country.
我创造了我们国家历史上最伟大的经济之一。

57
00:04:55,179 --> 00:04:56,780
I'll do it again and even better.
我会再次做到，甚至做得更好。

58
00:04:56,980 --> 00:05:03,551
We are going to get to immigration and border security during this debate, but I would like to let Vice President Harris respond on the economy here.
在本次辩论中，我们将讨论移民和边境安全，但我希望让副总统哈里斯在经济方面回应一下。

59
00:05:04,022 --> 00:05:05,263
Well, I would love to.
我很乐意。

60
00:05:05,343 --> 00:05:08,605
Let's talk about what Donald Trump left us.
让我们来谈谈唐纳德·特朗普留给我们的遗产。

61
00:05:09,345 --> 00:05:14,248
Donald Trump left us the worst unemployment since the Great Depression.
唐纳德·特朗普留给我们自大萧条以来最糟糕的失业率。

62
00:05:14,909 --> 00:05:20,552
Donald Trump left us the worst public health epidemic in a century.
唐纳德·特朗普留给我们一个世纪以来最严重的公共卫生流行病。

63
00:05:21,072 --> 00:05:27,917
Donald Trump left us the worst attack on our democracy since the Civil War.
唐纳德·特朗普留给我们自内战以来对民主的最严重攻击。

64
00:05:28,877 --> 00:05:32,061
And what we have done is clean up Donald Trump's mess.
而我们所做的就是清理唐纳德·特朗普留下的烂摊子。

65
00:05:32,681 --> 00:05:39,088
What we have done and what I intend to do is build on what we know are the aspirations and the hopes of the American people.
我们所做的，以及我打算做的，是建立在我们所知道的美国人民的愿望和希望之上。

66
00:05:39,108 --> 00:05:44,333
But I'm going to tell you on this debate tonight, you're going to hear from the same old tired playbook.
但我要告诉你，今晚的辩论中，你将听到同样老旧的剧本。

67
00:05:45,234 --> 00:05:48,298
A bunch of lies, grievances, and name-calling.
一堆谎言、抱怨和人身攻击。

68
00:05:48,778 --> 00:05:59,030
What you're going to hear tonight is a detailed and dangerous plan called Project 2025 that the former president intends on implementing if he were elected again.
你今晚要听到的是一个名为“2025计划”的详细而危险的计划，前总统打算在再次当选后实施。

69
00:06:00,171 --> 00:06:10,640
I believe very strongly that the American people want a president who understands the importance of bringing us together, knowing we have so much more in common than what separates us.
我非常坚信，美国人民希望有一位理解团结重要性的总统，知道我们之间有太多共同点，而不是分隔我们。

70
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:14,042
And I pledge to you to be a president for all Americans.
我向你们承诺，将成为所有美国人的总统。

71
00:06:14,243 --> 00:06:15,744
President Trump will give you a minute here to respond.
特朗普总统将在这里给你一分钟的时间回应。

72
00:06:16,044 --> 00:06:21,308
Number one, I have nothing to do, as you know, and as she knows better than anyone, I have nothing to do with Project 2025.
第一，我与2025计划没有任何关系，你知道的，她比任何人都更清楚，我与2025计划无关。

73
00:06:22,529 --> 00:06:23,290
That's out there.
那是存在的。

74
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:24,351
I haven't read it.
我没有读过它。

75
00:06:24,531 --> 00:06:25,952
I don't want to read it purposely.
我故意不想读它。

76
00:06:25,992 --> 00:06:26,872
I'm not going to read it.
我不会去读它。

77
00:06:27,193 --> 00:06:28,854
This was a group of people that got together.
这是一群人聚在一起。

78
00:06:28,914 --> 00:06:33,217
They came up with some ideas, I guess some good, some bad, but it makes no difference.
他们想出了一些想法，我想有些好，有些坏，但这没有关系。

79
00:06:33,257 --> 00:06:34,178
I have nothing to do.
我无事可做。

80
00:06:34,298 --> 00:06:35,659
Everybody knows I'm an open book.
大家都知道我是一开放的书。

81
00:06:35,739 --> 00:06:37,120
Everybody knows what I'm going to do.
大家都知道我将要做什么。

82
00:06:37,181 --> 00:06:41,444
Cut taxes very substantially and create a great economy like I did before.
大幅减税，创造出像我以前那样的伟大经济。

83
00:06:41,964 --> 00:06:43,365
We had the greatest economy.
我们曾拥有最伟大的经济。

84
00:06:43,405 --> 00:06:44,685
We got hit with a pandemic.
然后我们遭遇了一场疫情。

85
00:06:45,065 --> 00:06:49,807
And the pandemic was not since 1917, where 100 million people died.
这场疫情自1917年以来没有发生过，造成了一亿人死亡。

86
00:06:50,187 --> 00:06:51,328
Has there been anything like it?
有没有发生过类似的事情？

87
00:06:51,388 --> 00:06:53,589
We did a phenomenal job with the pandemic.
我们在应对疫情方面做得非常出色。

88
00:06:54,049 --> 00:07:01,692
We handed them over a country where the economy and where the stock market was higher than it was before the pandemic came in.
我们交给他们的是一个经济和股市都比疫情前更高的国家。

89
00:07:02,252 --> 00:07:03,872
Nobody's ever seen anything like it.
没有人见过这样的情况。

90
00:07:04,253 --> 00:07:06,553
We made ventilators for the entire world.
我们为全世界制造了呼吸机。

91
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:07,454
We got gowns.
我们有防护服。

92
00:07:07,514 --> 00:07:08,394
We got masks.
我们有口罩。

93
00:07:08,454 --> 00:07:10,335
We did things that nobody thought possible.
我们做了很多人认为不可能的事情。

94
00:07:10,815 --> 00:07:13,136
And people give me credit for rebuilding the military.
人们称赞我重建军队的成就。

95
00:07:13,156 --> 00:07:17,939
They give me credit for a lot of things, but not enough credit for the great job we did with the pandemic.
他们赞扬我做了很多事情，但对我们在疫情中所做的伟大工作却没有给予足够的认可。

96
00:07:18,239 --> 00:07:20,561
But the only jobs they got were bounce-back jobs.
但他们得到的只是反弹型工作。

97
00:07:20,581 --> 00:07:24,823
These were jobs bounce-back, and it bounced back and it went to their benefit.
这些是反弹型工作，它们反弹了，并且对他们有利。

98
00:07:25,183 --> 00:07:26,844
But I was the one that created them.
但我才是创造这些工作的那个人。

99
00:07:26,964 --> 00:07:28,705
They know it, and so does everybody else.
他们知道，我想大家都知道。

100
00:07:28,805 --> 00:07:29,986
Vice President Harris, I'll let you respond.
哈里斯副总统，我让你回应。

101
00:07:32,662 --> 00:07:34,163
Donald Trump has no plan for you.
唐纳德·特朗普没有为你们准备任何计划。

102
00:07:35,304 --> 00:07:39,947
And when you look at his economic plan, it's all about tax breaks for the richest people.
当你看看他的经济计划时，全部都是为最富有的人减税。

103
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:52,157
I am offering what I describe as an opportunity economy, and the best economists in our country, if not the world, have reviewed our relative plans for the future of America.
我提供的是我所描述的机会经济，我们国家，甚至是全球最优秀的经济学家们都审视了我们对美国未来的相对计划。

104
00:07:52,877 --> 00:08:00,043
What Goldman Sachs has said is that Donald Trump's plan would make the economy worse, mine would strengthen the economy.
高盛所说的是，唐纳德·特朗普的计划会使经济变得更糟，而我的计划则会加强经济。

105
00:08:00,484 --> 00:08:06,809
What the Wharton School has said is Donald Trump's plan would actually explode the deficit.
沃顿商学院表示，特朗普的计划实际上会导致财政赤字激增。

106
00:08:07,349 --> 00:08:17,378
Sixteen Nobel laureates have described his economic plan as something that would increase inflation and by the middle of next year would invite a recession.
十六位诺贝尔奖得主形容他的经济计划将增加通货膨胀，并且到明年年中将引发衰退。

107
00:08:18,078 --> 00:08:22,024
You just have to look at where we are and where we stand on the issues.
你只需看看我们现在的状况以及我们在这些问题上的立场。

108
00:08:22,064 --> 00:08:31,297
And I'd invite you to know that Donald Trump actually has no plan for you, because he is more interested in defending himself than he is in looking out for you.
我想让你知道，特朗普实际上没有为你们制定计划，因为他更关心的是为自己辩护，而不是为你们着想。

109
00:08:32,034 --> 00:08:33,015
It's just a soundbite.
这只是一个口号。

110
00:08:33,095 --> 00:08:41,421
They gave her that to say, look, I went to the Wharton School of Finance and many of those professors, the top professors think my plan is a brilliant plan.
他们让她说，看，我上过沃顿商学院，许多顶尖教授认为我的计划是一个绝妙的计划。

111
00:08:41,481 --> 00:08:42,221
It's a great plan.
这是一个很棒的计划。

112
00:08:42,301 --> 00:08:46,264
It's a plan that's going to bring up our worth, our value as a country.
这是一个将提升我们作为国家价值的计划。

113
00:08:46,324 --> 00:08:49,186
It's going to make people want to be able to go and work and
这将使人们愿意去工作，

114
00:08:49,746 --> 00:08:55,011
and create jobs and create a lot of good, solid money for our country.
创造就业机会，为我们的国家创造大量稳定的财富。

115
00:08:55,512 --> 00:08:58,855
Just to finish off, she doesn't have a plan.
最后，她没有计划。

116
00:08:59,235 --> 00:09:09,465
She copied Biden's plan, and it's like four sentences, like run, spot, run, four sentences that are just, oh, we'll try and lower taxes.
她抄袭了拜登的计划，就像四句话，像“跑，点，跑”，四句话只是说，哦，我们会试着减税。

117
00:09:09,985 --> 00:09:10,806
She doesn't have a plan.
她没有计划。

118
00:09:10,826 --> 00:09:11,647
Take a look at her plan.
看看她的计划。

119
00:09:11,887 --> 00:09:12,828
She doesn't have a plan.
她没有计划。

120
00:09:13,737 --> 00:09:16,199
Mr. President, I do want to drill down on something you both brought up.
总统先生，我确实想深入讨论你们两位提到的一个问题。

