我说，我想这会很盛大

620
00:44:17,211 --> 00:44:23,535
I went to Nancy Pelosi and the mayor of Washington, D.C., and the mayor put it back in writing, as you know.
我去找南希·佩洛西和华盛顿特区的市长，市长如你所知，写下了

621
00:44:24,236 --> 00:44:28,658
I said, you know, this is going to be a very big rally or whatever you want to call it.
我说，你知道，这将是一个非常盛大的集会，或者你想称之为什么

622
00:44:29,039 --> 00:44:30,579
And again, it wasn't done by me.
而且，这不是我做的

623
00:44:30,599 --> 00:44:31,400
It was done by others.
这是其他人做的

624
00:44:31,820 --> 00:44:35,803
I said, I'd like to give you 10,000 National Guard or soldiers.
我说，我想给你们提供1万名国民警卫队或士兵

625
00:44:36,383 --> 00:44:37,283
They rejected me.
他们拒绝了我。

626
00:44:37,343 --> 00:44:39,004
Nancy Pelosi rejected me.
南希·佩洛西拒绝了我。

627
00:44:39,084 --> 00:44:40,725
It was just two weeks ago.
就在两周前。

628
00:44:40,785 --> 00:44:45,027
Her daughter has a tape of her saying she is fully responsible for what happened.
她的女儿有一段录音，里面说她对发生的事情负全责。

629
00:44:45,347 --> 00:44:46,387
They want to get rid of that tape.
他们想要销毁那段录音。

630
00:44:47,247 --> 00:44:51,849
It would have never happened if Nancy Pelosi and the mayor of Washington did their jobs.
如果南希·佩洛西和华盛顿市长履行他们的职责，这一切就不会发生。

631
00:44:52,290 --> 00:44:54,030
I wasn't responsible for security.
我对安全问题不负责任。

632
00:44:54,370 --> 00:44:56,291
Nancy Pelosi was responsible.
南希·佩洛西负责。

633
00:44:56,531 --> 00:44:57,512
She didn't do her job.
她没有做好她的工作。

634
00:44:57,772 --> 00:45:00,893
The question was about you as president, not about former Speaker Pelosi.
问题是关于你作为总统的，而不是关于前众议院议长佩洛西。

635
00:45:00,933 --> 00:45:02,794
But I do want Vice President Harris to respond here.
但我确实希望哈里斯副总统在这里回应。

636
00:45:04,787 --> 00:45:06,507
I was at the Capitol on January 6th.
我在1月6日那天在国会大厦。

637
00:45:07,328 --> 00:45:09,548
I was the vice president-elect.
我当时是副总统当选人。

638
00:45:09,608 --> 00:45:11,328
I was also an acting senator.
我也是一名代理参议员。

639
00:45:11,609 --> 00:45:12,069
I was there.
我在那里。

640
00:45:13,049 --> 00:45:25,532
And on that day, the President of the United States incited a violent mob to attack our nation's Capitol, to desecrate our nation's Capitol.
在那一天，美国总统煽动了一群暴徒攻击我们国家的国会大厦，亵渎我们的国会大厦。

641
00:45:25,692 --> 00:45:30,813
On that day, 140 law enforcement officers were injured, and some died.
在那一天，140名执法人员受伤，一些人甚至丧生。

642
00:45:32,017 --> 00:45:38,940
And understand, the former president has been indicted and impeached for exactly that reason.
而且要明白，前总统正是因为这个原因被起诉和弹劾。

643
00:45:39,801 --> 00:45:42,122
But this is not an isolated situation.
但这并不是孤立的情况。

644
00:45:42,782 --> 00:45:52,527
Let's remember Charlottesville, where there was a mob of people carrying tiki torches, spewing anti-Semitic hate.
让我们回想一下夏洛茨维尔，当时有一群人挥舞着火把，散播反犹太主义仇恨。

645
00:45:53,667 --> 00:45:56,749
And what did the president then at the time say?
那么当时的总统说了什么呢？

646
00:45:56,769 --> 00:45:59,150
There were fine people on each side.
他说双方都有好人。

647
00:45:59,990 --> 00:46:00,731
Let's remember.
让我们记住。

648
00:46:01,738 --> 00:46:09,708
that when it came to the Proud Boys, a militia, the president said, the former president said, stand back and stand by.
当谈到骄傲男孩，一个民兵组织时，总统曾说，前总统说，退后并待命。

649
00:46:10,770 --> 00:46:18,019
So for everyone watching who remembers what January 6th was, I say we don't have to go back.
所以对于所有观看的人，记得1月6日发生的事情，我想说我们不必回头。

650
00:46:19,099 --> 00:46:20,060
Let's not go back.
让我们不要回头。

651
00:46:20,100 --> 00:46:21,181
We're not going back.
我们不会回头。

652
00:46:21,542 --> 00:46:23,163
It's time to turn the page.
是时候翻开新的一页了。

653
00:46:24,104 --> 00:46:40,041
And if that was a bridge too far for you, well, there is a place in our campaign for you to stand for country, to stand for our democracy, to stand for rule of law, and to end the chaos
如果这对你来说太过分了，那么在我们的竞选中有一个地方可以让你为国家而战，为我们的民主而战，为法治而战，并结束这种混乱

654
00:46:41,195 --> 00:46:49,079
and to end the approach that is about attacking the foundations of our democracy, because you don't like the outcome.
以及结束那种攻击我们民主基础的做法，因为你不喜欢结果。

655
00:46:49,439 --> 00:46:51,480
And be clear on that point.
对此要明确。

656
00:46:51,900 --> 00:47:00,564
Donald Trump, the candidate, has said in this election there will be a bloodbath if this and the outcome of this election is not to his liking.
唐纳德·特朗普，这位候选人，在这次选举中表示，如果这次选举的结果不如他所愿，将会是一场血腥的屠杀。

657
00:47:01,874 --> 00:47:03,215
Let's turn the page on this.
让我们翻开新的一页。

658
00:47:03,495 --> 00:47:04,476
Let's not go back.
让我们不要回头。

659
00:47:04,996 --> 00:47:10,599
Let's chart a course for the future and not go backwards to the past.
让我们为未来制定一条道路，而不是回到过去。

660
00:47:10,979 --> 00:47:11,980
Let me just follow up here.
让我在这里跟进一下。

661
00:47:13,160 --> 00:47:19,104
It was a different term, and it was a term that related to energy, because they have destroyed our energy business.
这是一个不同的术语，涉及到能源，因为他们摧毁了我们的能源产业。

662
00:47:19,144 --> 00:47:20,385
That was where Bloodbath was.
那就是血腥屠杀的来源。

663
00:47:20,745 --> 00:47:24,847
Also, on Charlottesville, that story has been, as you would say, debunked.
此外，关于夏洛茨维尔的故事，正如你所说，已经被揭穿。

664
00:47:25,327 --> 00:47:26,268
Laura Ingram,
劳拉·英格拉姆，

665
00:47:26,508 --> 00:47:30,672
Sean Hannity, Jesse, all of these people, they covered it.
肖恩·汉尼提，杰西，所有这些人，他们都报道了这个。

666
00:47:30,953 --> 00:47:33,976
If they go an extra sentence, they will see it was perfect.
如果他们多说一句话，他们会看到这是完美的。

667
00:47:34,356 --> 00:47:40,062
It was debunked in almost every newspaper, but they still bring it up, just like they bring 2025 up.
几乎所有报纸都揭穿了这个，但他们仍然提起，就像他们提起2025一样。

668
00:47:40,443 --> 00:47:41,604
They bring all of this stuff up.
他们提起所有这些事情。

669
00:47:41,884 --> 00:47:44,246
I ask you this, you talk about the Capitol.
我问你，你谈到国会大厦。

670
00:47:45,067 --> 00:47:49,749
Why are we allowing these millions of people to come through on the southern border?
为什么我们让这些数百万的人通过南部边界？

671
00:47:49,769 --> 00:47:51,050
How come she's not doing anything?
她为什么不采取任何行动？

672
00:47:51,310 --> 00:47:54,031
And I'll tell you what I would do, and I would be very proud to do it.
我告诉你我会怎么做，我会非常自豪地去做。

673
00:47:54,571 --> 00:47:57,493
I would say we would both leave this debate right now.
我会说我们现在就离开这场辩论。

674
00:47:58,093 --> 00:47:59,394
I'd like to see her go down
我想看看她去

675
00:48:00,194 --> 00:48:01,394
to Washington D.C.
华盛顿特区。

676
00:48:01,454 --> 00:48:09,076
during this debate, because we're wasting a lot of time, go down to, because she's been so bad, it's so ridiculous, go down to Washington D.C.
在这场辩论期间，因为我们浪费了很多时间，去华盛顿特区，因为她表现得太糟糕，太荒谬了，去华盛顿特区。

677
00:48:09,356 --> 00:48:11,817
and let her sign a bill to close up the border.
让她签署一项法案来关闭边境

678
00:48:12,077 --> 00:48:13,617
Because they have the right to do it.
因为他们有权这样做

679
00:48:13,657 --> 00:48:14,578
They don't need bills.
他们不需要法案

680
00:48:14,938 --> 00:48:15,918
They have the right to do it.
他们有权这样做

681
00:48:15,938 --> 00:48:23,320
The President of the United States, you'll get him out of bed, you'll wake him up at 4 o'clock in the afternoon, you'll say, come on, come on down to the office, let's sign a bill.
美国总统，你可以把他叫起来，下午四点叫醒他，告诉他，快来办公室，签署一项法案

682
00:48:23,860 --> 00:48:30,324
If he signs a bill that the border is closed, all he has to do is say it to the border patrol, who are phenomenal.
如果他签署一项关闭边境的法案，他只需要告诉边境巡逻队，他们非常出色

683
00:48:30,764 --> 00:48:33,046
If they do that, the border is closed.
如果他们这样做，边境就会关闭

684
00:48:33,086 --> 00:48:36,328
Those people are killing many people, unlike J6.
那些人正在杀死许多人，不像一月六日那样

685
00:48:36,348 --> 00:48:37,569
We talked immigration here tonight.
我们今晚讨论了移民问题

686
00:48:37,609 --> 00:48:44,393
I do want to focus on this next issue to both of you, because it really brings us, this into focus, truth in these times that we're living in.
我确实想关注下一个问题，因为这让我们更清晰地认识到我们生活时代的真相

687
00:48:45,073 --> 00:48:53,395
Mr. President, for three and a half years after you lost the 2020 election, you repeatedly falsely claimed that you won, many times saying you won in a landslide.
总统先生，在您输掉2020年选举后的三年半里，您多次错误地声称自己获胜，很多次说您是以压倒性优势获胜的

688
00:48:53,875 --> 00:49:01,956
In the past couple of weeks leading up to this debate, you have said, quote, you lost by a whisker, that you, quote, didn't quite make it, that you came up a little bit short.
在这场辩论前的几周里，您曾说过，引用，您输得很微弱，引用，您，引用，没能完全做到，稍微有点差距

689
00:49:02,476 --> 00:49:02,996
I said that?
我说过那样的话？

690
00:49:03,216 --> 00:49:05,257
Are you now acknowledging that you lost in 2020?
您现在承认您在2020年输了？

691
00:49:05,317 --> 00:49:06,877
No, I don't acknowledge that at all.
不，我一点也不承认

692
00:49:06,897 --> 00:49:07,317
But you did say that.
但您确实说过那样的话

693
00:49:07,337 --> 00:49:08,217
I said that sarcastically.
我是讽刺地说的

694
00:49:08,257 --> 00:49:08,717
You know that.
您知道的

695
00:49:09,177 --> 00:49:10,718
We said, oh, we lost by a whisker.
我们说，哦，我们输得很微弱

696
00:49:10,978 --> 00:49:12,238
That was said sarcastically.
那是讽刺地说的

697
00:49:13,678 --> 00:49:14,618
There's so much proof.
有很多证据

698
00:49:14,818 --> 00:49:16,159
All you have to do is look at it.
您所要做的就是看看

699
00:49:16,379 --> 00:49:19,420
And they should have sent it back to the legislatures for approval.
他们应该把它送回立法机构批准

700
00:49:19,820 --> 00:49:24,281
I got almost 75 million votes, the most votes any sitting president has ever gotten.
我得到了将近7500万票，任何现任总统获得的最多选票

701
00:49:24,321 --> 00:49:28,963
I was told if I got 63, which was what I got in 2016, you can't be beaten.
我被告知如果我得到63万票，也就是我在2016年得到的，您就不能被击败

702
00:49:29,783 --> 00:49:33,746
The election people should never be thinking about an election is fraudulent.
选举人员绝不能认为选举是欺诈的

703
00:49:33,766 --> 00:49:34,607
We need two things.
我们需要两件事

704
00:49:34,667 --> 00:49:37,529
We need walls We need and we have to have it.
我们需要墙，我们必须有。

705
00:49:37,809 --> 00:49:45,054
We have to have borders and we have to have good elections Our elections are bad and a lot of these illegal immigrants coming in.
我们必须有边界，并且我们必须有良好的选举。我们的选举很糟糕，很多非法移民正是这样进入的。

706
00:49:45,314 --> 00:49:46,816
They're trying to get them to vote.
他们试图让他们投票。

707
00:49:46,876 --> 00:49:55,662
They can't even speak English They don't even know what country they're in practically and these people are trying to get them to vote and that's why they're allowing Them to come into our country
他们甚至不会说英语，几乎不知道自己在哪个国家，而这些人在试图让他们投票，这就是为什么他们允许这些人进入我们的国家。

708
00:49:55,862 --> 00:49:57,644
You should watch all of these pieces of video.
你应该观看所有这些视频片段。

709
00:49:58,405 --> 00:49:59,726
I didn't detect the sarcasm.
我没有察觉到讽刺。

710
00:49:59,766 --> 00:50:00,547
Lost by a whisker.
差一点就输了。

711
00:50:00,567 --> 00:50:01,428
We didn't quite make it.
我们没有完全成功。

712
00:50:01,948 --> 00:50:08,675
And we should just point out here, as clarification, and you know this, you and your allies, 60 cases in front of many judges, many of them Republican, and said there was no widespread fraud.
在这里我们需要澄清一点，你和你的盟友都知道，有60个案件提交给许多法官，其中许多是共和党人，他们说没有广泛的欺诈。

713
00:50:08,695 --> 00:50:09,256
No judge looked at it.
没有法官对此进行审查。

714
00:50:09,276 --> 00:50:10,517
They said we didn't have standing.
他们说我们没有法律地位。

715
00:50:10,938 --> 00:50:11,678
That's the other thing.
这就是另外一件事。

716
00:50:12,239 --> 00:50:14,662
They said we didn't have standing, a technicality.
他们说我们没有法律地位，这是一个技术性问题。

717
00:50:14,882 --> 00:50:19,426
Can you imagine a system where a person in an election doesn't have standing?
你能想象在一个选举中，一个人没有法律地位的系统吗？

718
00:50:19,466 --> 00:50:22,570
The President of the United States doesn't have standing.
美国总统没有法律地位。

719
00:50:22,910 --> 00:50:23,871
That's how we lost.
这就是我们失败的原因。

720
00:50:24,371 --> 00:50:27,775
If you look at the facts, and I'd love to have you do a special on it,
如果你看一下事实，我很乐意让你做一个特别节目，

721
00:50:28,215 --> 00:50:36,000
I'll show you Georgia, and I'll show you Wisconsin, and I'll show you Pennsylvania, and I'll show you — we have so many facts and statistics.
我会给你展示乔治亚州，我会给你展示威斯康星州，我会给你展示宾夕法尼亚州，我会给你展示——我们有很多事实和统计数据。

722
00:50:36,281 --> 00:50:36,881
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

723
00:50:37,161 --> 00:50:40,723
That doesn't matter, because we have to solve the problem that we have right now.
这并不重要，因为我们必须解决我们现在面临的问题。

724
00:50:40,784 --> 00:50:41,684
That's old news.
那是旧闻。

725
00:50:42,064 --> 00:50:48,989
And the problem that we have right now is we have a nation in decline, and they have put it into decline.
而我们现在面临的问题是我们有一个正在衰退的国家，而他们让它陷入衰退。

726
00:50:49,329 --> 00:50:51,851
We have a nation that is dying, David.
我们有一个正在死亡的国家，大卫。

727
00:50:51,991 --> 00:50:53,031
Mr. President, thank you.
总统先生，谢谢您。

728
00:50:53,432 --> 00:50:55,813
Vice President Harris, you heard the president there tonight.
哈里斯副总统，您今晚听到了总统的讲话。

729
00:50:55,933 --> 00:50:57,713
He said he didn't say that, that he lost by a whisker.
他说他没有这么说，而是以微弱的差距输掉了。

730
00:50:57,733 --> 00:51:04,396
So he still believes he did not lose the election that was won by President Biden and yourself.
所以他仍然相信他没有输给拜登总统和你赢得的选举。

731
00:51:05,136 --> 00:51:07,817
But I do want to ask you about something that's come up in the last couple of days.
但我确实想问你关于最近几天出现的事情。

732
00:51:07,837 --> 00:51:09,598
This was a post from President Trump.
这是特朗普总统的一条帖子。

733
00:51:10,218 --> 00:51:12,421
about this upcoming election just weeks away.
关于即将到来的选举，仅有几周的时间。

734
00:51:12,461 --> 00:51:22,891
He said, when I win, those people who cheated, and then he lists donors, voters, election officials, he says, will be prosecuted to the fullest extent of the law, which will include long-term prison sentences.
他说，当我赢的时候，那些作弊的人，然后他列出了捐赠者、选民和选举官员，他说，将会依法追究，可能会面临长期监禁。

735
00:51:23,532 --> 00:51:27,416
One of your campaign's top lawyers responded, saying, we won't let Donald Trump intimidate us.
你们竞选团队的一位高级律师回应说，我们不会让唐纳德·特朗普威胁我们。

736
00:51:27,776 --> 00:51:29,578
We won't let him suppress the vote.
我们不会让他压制投票。

737
00:51:30,078 --> 00:51:31,560
Is that what you believe he's trying to do here?
你认为他在这里想要做的就是这个吗？

738
00:51:33,311 --> 00:51:36,094
Donald Trump was fired by 81 million people.
唐纳德·特朗普被8100万民众解雇。

739
00:51:36,915 --> 00:51:38,256
So let's be clear about that.
所以让我们对此明确一下。

740
00:51:38,577 --> 00:51:41,760
And clearly he is having a very difficult time processing that.
显然他在处理这个问题时非常困难。

741
00:51:42,714 --> 00:51:54,958
But we cannot afford to have a President of the United States who attempts, as he did in the past, to upend the will of the voters in a free and fair election.
但我们不能容忍一位美国总统像他过去那样试图颠覆自由公正选举中的选民意愿。

742
00:51:55,738 --> 00:52:04,121
And I'm going to tell you that I have traveled the world as Vice President of the United States, and world leaders are laughing at Donald Trump.
我告诉你，作为美国副总统，我周游世界，世界领导人在嘲笑唐纳德·特朗普。

743
00:52:04,981 --> 00:52:10,443
I have talked with military leaders, some of whom worked with you, and they say you're a disgrace.
我和一些曾与你合作的军事领导人交谈过，他们说你是个耻辱。

744
00:52:11,703 --> 00:52:31,652
And when you then talk in this way in a presidential debate and deny what over and over again are court cases you have lost because you did in fact lose that election, it leads one to believe that perhaps we do not have in the candidate to my right the temperament
当你在总统辩论中以这种方式发言，并否认你一再输掉的法庭案件，因为你实际上输掉了那场选举，这让人相信，也许我右边的候选人没有

745
00:52:32,834 --> 00:52:37,418
or the ability to not be confused about fact.
或缺乏不对事实感到困惑的能力。

746
00:52:37,959 --> 00:52:41,582
That's deeply troubling, and the American people deserve better.
这非常令人不安，美国人民值得更好的。

747
00:52:42,463 --> 00:52:43,844
I'll give you one minute to respond, Mr. President.
我给你一分钟时间回应，总统先生。

748
00:52:43,904 --> 00:52:45,265
Let me just tell you about world leaders.
让我告诉你关于世界领导人的事情。

749
00:52:45,826 --> 00:52:48,128
Viktor Orban, one of the most respected men.
维克托·欧尔班，最受尊敬的人之一。

750
00:52:48,328 --> 00:52:49,409
They call him a strong man.
他们称他为强人。

751
00:52:49,449 --> 00:52:50,770
He's a tough person.
他是个强硬的人。

752
00:52:51,551 --> 00:52:51,931
Smart.
聪明。

753
00:52:52,472 --> 00:52:53,653
Prime Minister of Hungary.
匈牙利总理。

754
00:52:54,173 --> 00:52:56,715
They said, why is the whole world blowing up?
他们说，为什么整个世界都在崩溃？

755
00:52:56,795 --> 00:52:57,956
Three years ago, it wasn't.
三年前，情况并非如此

756
00:52:58,016 --> 00:52:59,077
Why is it blowing up?
为什么会突然爆发？

757
00:52:59,778 --> 00:53:03,481
He said, because you need Trump back as president.
他说，因为你需要特朗普回到总统的位置。

758
00:53:04,022 --> 00:53:05,083
They were afraid of him.
他们害怕他。

759
00:53:05,183 --> 00:53:06,264
China was afraid.
中国害怕。

760
00:53:06,324 --> 00:53:08,746
And I don't like to use the word afraid, but I'm just quoting him.
我不喜欢用“害怕”这个词，但我只是引用他的话。

761
00:53:09,286 --> 00:53:10,447
China was afraid of him.
中国害怕他。

762
00:53:10,868 --> 00:53:12,469
North Korea was afraid of him.
北朝鲜害怕他。

763
00:53:12,909 --> 00:53:14,971
Look at what's going on with North Korea, by the way.
顺便说一下，看看北朝鲜发生了什么。

764
00:53:15,291 --> 00:53:17,013
He said Russia was afraid of him.
他说俄罗斯害怕他。

765
00:53:17,393 --> 00:53:23,659
I ended the Nord Stream 2 pipeline and Biden put it back on day one, but he ended the XL pipeline.
我结束了北溪2号管道，而拜登在第一天就让它恢复，但他结束了XL管道。

766
00:53:24,239 --> 00:53:33,908
The XL pipeline in our country, he ended that, but he let the Russians build a pipeline going all over Europe and heading into Germany, the biggest pipeline in the world.
在我们国家，XL管道被他终止，但他却让俄罗斯人在欧洲建造一条通往德国的管道，这条管道是世界上最大的。

767
00:53:34,288 --> 00:53:34,469
Look.
看。

768
00:53:35,430 --> 00:53:37,531
Victor Orban said it.
维克托·欧尔班说过。

769
00:53:37,911 --> 00:53:42,192
He said the most respected, most feared person is Donald Trump.
他说，最受尊敬、最令人畏惧的人是唐纳德·特朗普。

770
00:53:42,532 --> 00:53:45,253
We had no problems when Trump was president.
当特朗普担任总统时，我们没有任何问题。

771
00:53:45,673 --> 00:53:53,835
But when this weak, pathetic man that you saw at a debate just a few months ago, that if he weren't in that debate, he'd be running instead of her.
但当你在几个月前看到的那个软弱可怜的人出现在辩论中时，如果他没有参加辩论，他本来会取代她。

772
00:53:53,875 --> 00:53:54,695
She got no votes.
她没有获得任何选票。

773
00:53:54,955 --> 00:53:56,315
He got 14 million votes.
他得到了1400万票。

774
00:53:56,355 --> 00:53:58,836
What you did, you talk about a threat to democracy.
你们谈论对民主的威胁。

775
00:53:59,376 --> 00:54:02,077
He got 14 million votes and they threw him out of office.
他得到了1400万票，他们却把他赶出了办公室。

776
00:54:02,737 --> 00:54:03,217
And you know what?
你知道吗？

777
00:54:03,237 --> 00:54:04,198
I'll give you a little secret.
我给你一个小秘密。

778
00:54:04,258 --> 00:54:04,978
He hates her.
他讨厌她。

779
00:54:05,259 --> 00:54:06,299
He can't stand her.
他受不了她。

780
00:54:06,820 --> 00:54:08,541
But he got 14 million votes.
但他得到了1400万票。

781
00:54:08,901 --> 00:54:09,802
They threw him out.
他们把他赶了出去。

782
00:54:10,202 --> 00:54:11,543
She got zero votes.
她没有获得任何选票。

783
00:54:11,843 --> 00:54:16,005
And when she ran, she was the first one to leave because she failed.
当她参选时，她是第一个因为失败而退场的人。

784
00:54:16,406 --> 00:54:17,406
And now she's running.
现在她又在竞选了。

785
00:54:17,747 --> 00:54:19,808
I don't understand it, but I'm okay with it because...
我不理解，但我对此没意见，因为…

786
00:54:20,208 --> 00:54:20,628
Your time is up.
你的时间到了。

787
00:54:20,648 --> 00:54:20,828
Thank you.
谢谢。

788
00:54:20,848 --> 00:54:21,688
I think we're going to do very well.
我认为我们会做得很好。

789
00:54:21,708 --> 00:54:22,809
We've got a lot more to get to.
我们还有很多事情要讨论。

790
00:54:22,849 --> 00:54:28,230
Turning now to the Israel-Hamas war and the hostages who are still being held, Americans among them.
现在转向以色列-哈马斯战争以及仍然被扣为人质的美国人。

791
00:54:28,590 --> 00:54:32,810
Vice President Harris, in December you said, quote, Israel has a right to defend itself.
哈里斯副总统，您在12月曾表示，以色列有权自卫。

792
00:54:32,870 --> 00:54:38,331
But you added, quote, it matters how, saying international humanitarian law must be respected.
但您补充说，方法很重要，国际人道法必须受到尊重。

793
00:54:38,511 --> 00:54:41,132
Israel must do more to protect innocent civilians.
以色列必须采取更多措施来保护无辜平民。

794
00:54:41,672 --> 00:54:43,132
You said that nine months ago.
您是九个月前这么说的。

795
00:54:43,212 --> 00:54:45,033
Now an estimated 40,000 Palestinians are dead.
现在估计有40,000名巴勒斯坦人已死亡。

796
00:54:46,713 --> 00:54:48,914
Nearly 100 hostages remain.
近100名人质仍然被扣押。

797
00:54:49,314 --> 00:54:53,356
Just last week, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said there's not a deal in the making.
就在上周，内塔尼亚胡总理表示，尚未达成协议。

798
00:54:53,757 --> 00:54:56,458
President Biden has not been able to break through the stalemate.
拜登总统未能打破僵局。

799
00:54:56,798 --> 00:54:57,518
How would you do it?
您将如何解决？

800
00:54:58,839 --> 00:55:00,920
Well, let's understand how we got here.
好吧，让我们理解一下我们是如何走到这一步的。

801
00:55:01,560 --> 00:55:06,503
On October 7, Hamas, a terrorist organization,
10月7日，哈马斯，一个恐怖组织，

802
00:55:08,280 --> 00:55:14,446
slaughtered 1,200 Israelis, many of them young people who were simply attending a concert.
屠杀了1,200名以色列人，他们中的许多人只是参加了一场音乐会。

803
00:55:15,207 --> 00:55:17,049
Women were horribly raped.
女性遭受了可怕的强奸。

804
00:55:17,589 --> 00:55:22,514
And so absolutely, I said then, I say now, Israel has a right to defend itself.
所以，我当时说过，现在也这样说，以色列有权自卫。

805
00:55:22,574 --> 00:55:22,974
We would.
我们也是。

806
00:55:24,326 --> 00:55:32,076
And how it does so matters, because it is also true far too many innocent Palestinians have been killed.
而且它的自卫方式很重要，因为同样有太多无辜的巴勒斯坦人被杀。

807
00:55:32,918 --> 00:55:33,959
Children, mothers.
孩子们，母亲们。

808
00:55:34,980 --> 00:55:38,445
What we know is that this war must end.
我们知道，这场战争必须结束。

809
00:55:39,326 --> 00:55:46,450
It must end immediately, and the way it will end is we need a ceasefire deal and we need the hostages out.
它必须立即结束，结束的方式是我们需要达成停火协议，并且要让人质获释。

810
00:55:47,210 --> 00:55:50,372
And so we will continue to work around the clock on that.
因此，我们将继续昼夜不息地努力。

811
00:55:51,152 --> 00:55:56,715
Work around the clock also understanding that we must chart a course for a two-state solution.
在昼夜不息的工作中，我们也必须为两国解决方案制定一条道路。

812
00:55:57,475 --> 00:56:05,563
And in that solution, there must be security for the Israeli people and Israel and an equal measure for the Palestinians.
在这个解决方案中，必须确保以色列人民和以色列的安全，同时也要给巴勒斯坦人同等的保障。

813
00:56:06,044 --> 00:56:19,398
But the one thing I will assure you always, I will always give Israel the ability to defend itself, in particular as it relates to Iran and any threat that Iran and its proxies pose to Israel.
但我可以向你们保证，我将始终赋予以色列自我防卫的能力，特别是涉及到伊朗及其代理人对以色列构成的威胁时。

814
00:56:19,938 --> 00:56:30,444
But we must have a two-state solution where we can rebuild Gaza, where the Palestinians have security, self-determination, and the dignity they so rightly deserve.
但我们必须有一个两国解决方案，让我们能够重建加沙，让巴勒斯坦人拥有安全、自决以及他们应有的尊严。

815
00:56:31,344 --> 00:56:40,829
President Trump, how would you negotiate with Netanyahu and also Hamas in order to get the hostages out and prevent the killing of more innocent civilians in Gaza?
特朗普总统，您将如何与内塔尼亚胡和哈马斯进行谈判，以便让人质获释并防止更多无辜平民在加沙被杀？

816
00:56:41,149 --> 00:56:43,471
If I were president, it would have never started.
如果我是总统，这一切根本不会开始。

817
00:56:43,991 --> 00:56:57,122
If I were president, Russia would have never, ever, I know Putin very well, he would have never, and there was no threat of it either, by the way, for four years, have gone into Ukraine and killed millions of people when you add it up.
如果我是总统，俄罗斯绝对不会，也从来没有，我非常了解普京，他绝不会，而且在那四年里根本没有这样的威胁，进入乌克兰并杀死数百万人。

818
00:56:57,402 --> 00:56:59,784
Far worse than people understand what's going on over there.
远比人们理解的情况要糟糕得多。

819
00:57:00,805 --> 00:57:05,070
But when she mentions about Israel, all of a sudden, she hates Israel.
但当她提到以色列时，突然之间，她就仇恨以色列。

820
00:57:05,371 --> 00:57:10,797
She wouldn't even meet with Netanyahu when he went to Congress to make a very important speech.
当内塔尼亚胡去国会发表非常重要的演讲时，她甚至不愿意见他。

821
00:57:11,078 --> 00:57:14,342
She refused to be there because she was at a sorority party of hers.
她拒绝出席，因为她正在参加自己的姐妹会聚会。

822
00:57:14,662 --> 00:57:16,164
She wanted to go to the sorority party.
她想去姐妹会聚会。

823
00:57:17,125 --> 00:57:18,085
She hates Israel.
她仇恨以色列。

824
00:57:18,545 --> 00:57:23,487
If she's president, I believe that Israel will not exist within two years from now.
如果她成为总统，我相信以色列在两年内将不复存在。

825
00:57:23,527 --> 00:57:26,408
And I've been pretty good at predictions, and I hope I'm wrong about that one.
而我在预测方面一向不错，我希望我在这一点上是错的。

826
00:57:27,088 --> 00:57:28,028
She hates Israel.
她仇恨以色列。

827
00:57:28,388 --> 00:57:36,890
At the same time, in her own way, she hates the Arab population, because the whole place is going to get blown up.
与此同时，以她自己的方式，她也仇恨阿拉伯人，因为整个地方将会被炸毁。

828
00:57:37,431 --> 00:57:40,411
Arabs, Jewish people, Israel.
阿拉伯人，犹太人，以色列。

829
00:57:40,732 --> 00:57:41,712
Israel will be gone.
以色列将会消失。

830
00:57:42,552 --> 00:57:44,094
It would have never happened.
这一切根本不会发生。

831
00:57:44,334 --> 00:57:46,536
Iran was broke under Donald Trump.
在特朗普任内，伊朗已经破产。

832
00:57:46,976 --> 00:57:51,901
Now Iran has $300 billion because they took off all the sanctions that I had.
现在伊朗有3000亿美元，因为他们取消了我施加的所有制裁。

833
00:57:52,301 --> 00:57:59,308
Iran had no money for Hamas or Hezbollah or any of the 28 different spheres of terror.
伊朗没有钱给哈马斯、真主党或其他28个恐怖领域

834
00:57:59,488 --> 00:58:02,069
And they are spheres of terror, horrible terror.
这些都是恐怖领域，令人恐惧的恐怖

835
00:58:02,450 --> 00:58:03,150
They had no money.
他们没有钱

836
00:58:03,530 --> 00:58:05,091
It was a big story, and you know it.
这是一个大新闻，你知道的

837
00:58:05,131 --> 00:58:06,712
You covered it very well, actually.
你实际上报道得很好

838
00:58:07,112 --> 00:58:09,213
They had no money for terror.
他们没有钱用于恐怖活动

839
00:58:09,653 --> 00:58:10,654
They were broke.
他们已经破产

840
00:58:11,074 --> 00:58:12,495
Now they're a rich nation.
现在他们是一个富裕的国家

841
00:58:12,735 --> 00:58:15,977
And now what they're doing is they're spreading that money around.
现在他们所做的是将这些钱四处散布

842
00:58:17,017 --> 00:58:20,020
Look at what's happening with the Houthis and Yemen.
看看胡塞武装和也门发生了什么

843
00:58:20,320 --> 00:58:22,082
Look at what's going on in the Middle East.
看看中东正在发生什么

844
00:58:22,542 --> 00:58:23,884
This would have never happened.
这一切绝对不会发生

845
00:58:24,164 --> 00:58:29,469
I will get that settled and fast, and I'll get the war with Ukraine and Russia ended.
我会迅速解决这个问题，并结束与乌克兰和俄罗斯的战争

846
00:58:30,089 --> 00:58:34,794
If I'm president-elect, I'll get it done before even becoming president.
如果我当选总统，我会在甚至成为总统之前就完成这件事

847
00:58:35,074 --> 00:58:37,297
Vice President Harris, he says you hate Israel.
哈里斯副总统，他说你讨厌以色列

848
00:58:38,098 --> 00:58:39,700
That's absolutely not true.
这绝对不是真的

849
00:58:39,720 --> 00:58:45,026
I have my entire career and life supported Israel and the Israeli people.
我在整个职业生涯和生活中都支持以色列和以色列人民

850
00:58:45,427 --> 00:58:46,108
He knows that.
他知道这一点

851
00:58:46,548 --> 00:58:49,993
He's trying to again divide and distract
他再次试图分裂和分散注意力

852
00:58:50,353 --> 00:58:58,858
from the reality, which is it is very well known that Donald Trump is weak and wrong on national security and foreign policy.
以掩盖现实，那就是唐纳德·特朗普在国家安全和外交政策上软弱和错误

853
00:58:59,018 --> 00:59:05,702
It is well known that he admires dictators, wants to be a dictator on day one according to himself.
众所周知，他崇拜独裁者，想要在第一天就成为独裁者

854
00:59:06,602 --> 00:59:14,965
It is well known that he said of Putin that he can do whatever the hell he wants and go into Ukraine.
众所周知，他曾说普京可以随心所欲地进入乌克兰

855
00:59:15,605 --> 00:59:20,867
It is well known that he said when Russia went into Ukraine, it was brilliant.
众所周知，他曾说当俄罗斯进入乌克兰时，这很聪明

856
00:59:21,867 --> 00:59:26,230
It is well known he exchanged love letters with Kim Jong-un.
众所周知，他和金正恩互换过情书

857
00:59:27,191 --> 00:59:40,681
And it is absolutely well known that these dictators and autocrats are rooting for you to be president again, because they're so clear they can manipulate you with flattery and favors.
而且众所周知，这些独裁者和专制者都希望你再次成为总统，因为他们很清楚可以用恭维和恩惠操控你

858
00:59:41,422 --> 00:59:42,543
And that is why
这就是原因

859
00:59:43,869 --> 00:59:49,172
So many military leaders who you have worked with have told me you are a disgrace.
你曾与之合作的许多军事领袖告诉我，你是个耻辱。

860
00:59:49,952 --> 01:00:03,880
That is why we understand that we have to have a president who is not consistently weak and wrong on national security, including the importance of upholding and respecting in highest regard our military.
这就是我们明白，我们需要一位在国家安全问题上不时软弱和错误的总统的原因，包括维护和尊重我们军队的重要性。

861
01:00:04,040 --> 01:00:05,321
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢您。

862
01:00:06,582 --> 01:00:08,484
And she's the one that caused it.
而她就是造成这一切的人。

863
01:00:08,904 --> 01:00:18,315
That's weak on national security by allowing every nation last month for the year 168 different countries sending people into our country.
在国家安全问题上软弱，允许上个月168个不同国家的人进入我们的国家。

864
01:00:18,575 --> 01:00:19,977
Their crime weights are way down.
他们的犯罪率显著下降。

865
01:00:20,918 --> 01:00:24,882
Putin endorsed her last week said I hope she wins and I think he meant it.
普京上周支持她，说我希望她赢，我认为他是认真的。

866
01:00:25,583 --> 01:00:28,886
because what he's gotten away with is absolutely incredible.
因为他所逃脱的事情简直令人难以置信。

867
01:00:28,926 --> 01:00:30,187
It wouldn't have happened with me.
这在我任内是不会发生的。

868
01:00:30,827 --> 01:00:35,851
The leaders of other countries think that they're weak and incompetent, and they are.
其他国家的领导人认为他们软弱和无能，而他们确实如此。

869
01:00:36,212 --> 01:00:37,633
They're grossly incompetent.
他们极其无能。

870
01:00:37,993 --> 01:00:39,494
And I just ask one question.
我只想问一个问题。

871
01:00:39,875 --> 01:00:50,964
Why does Biden go in and kill the Keystone pipeline and approve the single biggest deal that Russia's ever made, Nord Stream 2, the biggest pipeline anywhere in the world going to Germany and all over Europe?
为什么拜登去关闭基石管道，却批准了俄罗斯有史以来最大的交易，北溪2号，这是通往德国和整个欧洲的最大管道？

872
01:00:51,604 --> 01:00:53,746
because they're weak and they're ineffective.
因为他们软弱和无能。

873
01:00:54,106 --> 01:00:56,308
And Biden, by the way, gets paid a lot of money.
顺便说一下，拜登赚了很多钱。

874
01:00:56,328 --> 01:00:56,668
Thank you.
谢谢。

875
01:00:56,708 --> 01:00:58,150
We have a lot of issues to get to.
我们有很多问题要讨论。

876
01:00:58,310 --> 01:01:04,535
We'll be right back with much more of this historic ABC News presidential debate from the National Constitution Center right here in Philadelphia.
我们很快会带来更多来自费城国家宪法中心的历史性ABC新闻总统辩论。

877
01:01:04,635 --> 01:01:05,196
Back in a moment.
稍后回来。

878
01:01:06,497 --> 01:01:09,599
The ABC News presidential debate will continue after this.
ABC新闻总统辩论将在此之后继续。

879
01:01:17,742 --> 01:01:21,485
from the National Constitution Center in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.
来自宾夕法尼亚州费城的国家宪法中心。

880
01:01:22,205 --> 01:01:25,388
Here again, David Muir and Lindsay Davis.
再次欢迎，大卫·穆尔和林赛·戴维斯。

881
01:01:25,988 --> 01:01:29,051
Welcome back to this historic ABC News presidential debate tonight.
欢迎回到今晚的历史性ABC新闻总统辩论。

882
01:01:29,071 --> 01:01:31,413
We're going to continue here, and I want to turn to the war in Ukraine.
我们将继续讨论，我想转向乌克兰战争。

883
01:01:31,433 --> 01:01:33,895
We're now two and a half years into this conflict.
我们现在已经进入这场冲突两年半了。

884
01:01:33,935 --> 01:01:45,844
Mr. President, it has been the position of the Biden administration that we must defend Ukraine from Russia, from Vladimir Putin, to defend their sovereignty, their democracy, that it's in America's best interest to do so, arguing that if Putin wins,
总统先生，拜登政府的立场是我们必须保护乌克兰免受俄罗斯和普京的侵害，以维护他们的主权和民主，这符合美国的最佳利益，认为如果普京获胜，

885
01:01:46,244 --> 01:01:48,886
He may be emboldened to move even further into other countries.
他可能会更加大胆地进入其他国家。

886
01:01:49,506 --> 01:01:51,868
You have said you would solve this war in 24 hours.
你曾说过你会在24小时内解决这场战争。

887
01:01:51,908 --> 01:01:53,629
You said so just before the break tonight.
你今晚在休息之前刚说过。

888
01:01:54,030 --> 01:01:55,811
How exactly would you do that?
你到底会怎么做呢？

889
01:01:56,091 --> 01:01:57,812
And I want to ask you a very simple question tonight.
我今晚想问你一个非常简单的问题。

890
01:01:58,092 --> 01:02:00,414
Do you want Ukraine to win this war?
你希望乌克兰赢得这场战争吗？

891
01:02:01,034 --> 01:02:02,255
I want the war to stop.
我希望战争停止。

892
01:02:02,576 --> 01:02:08,239
I want to save lives that are being uselessly people being killed by the millions.
我想拯救那些毫无意义地被杀害的生命，数以百万计。

893
01:02:08,320 --> 01:02:09,160
It's the millions.
就是数以百万计。

894
01:02:09,560 --> 01:02:13,143
It's so much worse than the numbers that you're getting, which are fake numbers.
这比你所掌握的数字要严重得多，而那些都是虚假的数字。

895
01:02:13,823 --> 01:02:14,004
Look,
听着，

896
01:02:15,069 --> 01:02:24,273
We're in for 250 billion or more because they don't ask Europe, which is a much bigger beneficiary to getting this thing done than we are.
我们已经投入了2500亿美元或更多，因为他们没有像我们一样向欧洲寻求帮助，欧洲在解决这个问题上是更大的受益者。

897
01:02:25,154 --> 01:02:33,838
They're in for 150 billion dollars less because Biden and you don't have the courage to ask Europe like I did with NATO.
他们少投入了1500亿美元，因为拜登和你没有勇气像我对待北约那样向欧洲要求。

898
01:02:34,278 --> 01:02:38,220
They paid billions and billions, hundreds of billions of dollars when I said
当我说要么你们付款，要么我们就不再保护你们时，他们支付了数十亿、数十亿，数百亿美元。

899
01:02:38,820 --> 01:02:41,441
Either you pay up, or we're not going to protect you anymore.
这可能是他们不喜欢我而更喜欢软弱之人的原因之一。

900
01:02:41,501 --> 01:02:45,363
So that's maybe one of the reasons they don't like me as much as they like weak people.
但你看看发生了什么。

901
01:02:45,843 --> 01:02:48,365
But you take a look at what's happening.
我们已经投入了2500亿到2750亿美元。

902
01:02:48,685 --> 01:02:52,126
We're in for $250 to $275 billion.
他们则投入了100亿到150亿美元。

903
01:02:52,406 --> 01:02:53,767
They're into $100 to $150.
他们应该被迫平衡。

904
01:02:55,248 --> 01:02:57,789
They should be forced to equalize.
话虽如此，我想让战争得到解决。

905
01:02:58,089 --> 01:03:00,770
With that being said, I want to get the war settled.
我非常了解泽连斯基，也非常了解普京。

906
01:03:00,990 --> 01:03:03,652
I know Zelensky very well, and I know Putin very well.
我与他们有良好的关系，他们尊重

907
01:03:03,692 --> 01:03:05,893
I have a good relationship, and they respect
你的总统，好吗？

908
01:03:06,733 --> 01:03:07,974
your president, okay?
他们尊重我。

909
01:03:08,014 --> 01:03:08,935
They respect me.
他们不尊重拜登。

910
01:03:08,975 --> 01:03:10,156
They don't respect Biden.
他们不尊重拜登。

911
01:03:10,216 --> 01:03:11,277
How would you respect him?
你将如何尊重他？

912
01:03:11,557 --> 01:03:11,897
Why?
Why?

913
01:03:11,937 --> 01:03:12,638
For what reason?
出于什么原因？

914
01:03:12,998 --> 01:03:17,001
He hasn't even made a phone call in two years to Putin, hasn't spoken to anybody.
他连两年来都没有给普京打过一个电话，也没有和任何人交谈过。

915
01:03:17,301 --> 01:03:18,462
They don't even try and get it.
他们甚至都不试图去了解。

916
01:03:18,782 --> 01:03:21,104
That is a war that's dying to be settled.
那是一场急需解决的战争。

917
01:03:21,424 --> 01:03:24,046
I will get it settled before I even become president.
在我成为总统之前，我会解决这个问题。

918
01:03:24,086 --> 01:03:31,232
If I win, when I'm president-elect, and what I'll do is I'll speak to one, I'll speak to the other, I'll get them together.
如果我赢了，当我当选总统后，我会和他们两个人交谈，把他们聚在一起。

919
01:03:31,512 --> 01:03:33,213
That war would have never happened.
那场战争根本不会发生。

920
01:03:33,554 --> 01:03:36,236
And in fact, when I saw Putin after I left,
事实上，当我离开后见到普京时，

921
01:03:36,816 --> 01:03:40,197
Unfortunately, left because our country has gone to hell.
不幸的是，我离开的原因是我们的国家已经变得一团糟。

922
01:03:40,697 --> 01:03:44,478
But after I left, when I saw him building up soldiers, he did it after I left.
但在我离开后，当我看到他集结士兵时，他是在我离开后才这样做的。

923
01:03:45,118 --> 01:03:47,739
I said, oh, he must be negotiating.
我说，哦，他一定在谈判。

924
01:03:47,819 --> 01:03:49,980
It must be a good, strong point of negotiation.
这一定是一个良好、强有力的谈判点。

925
01:03:50,320 --> 01:03:54,121
Well, it wasn't because Biden had no idea how to talk to him.
但事实并非如此，因为拜登根本不知道如何和他交谈。

926
01:03:54,361 --> 01:03:56,121
He had no idea how to stop it.
他根本不知道如何阻止这一切。

927
01:03:56,421 --> 01:03:59,702
And now you have millions of people dead and it's only getting worse.
现在你有数百万人死去，情况只会变得更糟。

928
01:03:59,782 --> 01:04:01,463
And it could lead to World War Three.
这可能会导致第三次世界大战。

929
01:04:01,723 --> 01:04:02,783
Don't kid yourself, David.
别自欺欺人，戴维。

930
01:04:03,223 --> 01:04:08,826
We're playing with World War III, and we have a president that we don't even know if he's—where is our president?
我们正在玩弄第三次世界大战，而我们有一位总统，我们甚至不知道他——我们的总统在哪里？

931
01:04:09,106 --> 01:04:10,587
We don't even know if he's a president.
我们甚至不知道他是否是总统。

932
01:04:10,607 --> 01:04:13,629
And just to clarify here— They threw him out of a campaign like a dog.
为了澄清一下——他们把他像狗一样从竞选中赶了出去。

933
01:04:13,669 --> 01:04:14,389
We don't even know.
我们甚至不知道。

934
01:04:14,830 --> 01:04:15,750
Is he our president?
他是我们的总统吗？

935
01:04:16,070 --> 01:04:19,072
But we have a president— Mr. President— —that doesn't know he's alive.
但我们有一位总统——总统先生——

936
01:04:19,352 --> 01:04:19,973
Your time is up.
他甚至不知道自己活着。

937
01:04:20,773 --> 01:04:22,054
Just to clarify the question.
为了澄清这个问题。

938
01:04:22,694 --> 01:04:23,975
Do you believe it's in the U.S.
您认为乌克兰赢得这场战争符合美国的最佳利益吗，是还是不是？

939
01:04:24,075 --> 01:04:26,578
best interest for Ukraine to win this war, yes or no?
我认为美国的最佳利益是尽快结束这场战争。

940
01:04:26,598 --> 01:04:27,458
I think it's the U.S.
达成一个协议。

941
01:04:27,538 --> 01:04:30,681
best interest to get this war finished and just get it done.
因为我们必须停止所有这些生命的毁灭。

942
01:04:31,122 --> 01:04:32,082
Negotiate a deal.
我想请副总统哈里斯发表看法。

943
01:04:32,323 --> 01:04:37,007
Because we have to stop all of these human lives from being destroyed.
我想听听您对当前支持乌克兰的看法。

944
01:04:37,027 --> 01:04:38,628
I want to take this to Vice President Harris.
但作为指挥官，如果当选，您将如何处理与普京的关系？

945
01:04:38,648 --> 01:04:42,331
I want to get your thoughts on support for Ukraine in this moment.
这与我们现在看到的拜登总统的做法有什么不同吗？

946
01:04:42,612 --> 01:04:47,036
But also, as Commander-in-Chief, if elected, how would you deal with Vladimir Putin?
首先，重要的是提醒前总统，您不是在与乔·拜登竞选，而是在与我竞选。

947
01:04:47,116 --> 01:04:49,598
And would it be any different from what we're seeing from President Biden?
我相信唐纳德·特朗普之所以说这场战争会在24小时内结束，是因为他会选择放弃。

948
01:04:50,680 --> 01:04:56,200
Well, first of all, it's important to remind the former president you're not running against Joe Biden, you're running against me.
而这不是我们作为美国人的本色。

949
01:04:58,323 --> 01:05:04,266
I believe the reason that Donald Trump says that this war would be over within 24 hours is because he would just give it up.
我们需要了解这里发生了什么。

950
01:05:05,166 --> 01:05:06,927
And that's not who we are as Americans.
在俄罗斯试图通过武力改变领土边界、违反国际最重要的规则和规范之一——主权和领土完整的重要性之前，我实际上与泽连斯基会面了几天。

951
01:05:06,967 --> 01:05:08,428
Let's understand what happened here.
我与泽连斯基总统会面。

952
01:05:09,268 --> 01:05:26,497
I actually met with Zelensky a few days before Russia invaded, tried through force to change territorial boundaries, to defy one of the most important international rules and norms, which is the importance of sovereignty and territorial integrity.
我与他分享了关于如何自我防卫的美国情报。

953
01:05:27,037 --> 01:05:28,598
And I met with President Zelensky.
几天后，我前往北约的东部前线，前往波兰和罗马尼亚。

954
01:05:28,738 --> 01:05:32,441
I shared with him American intelligence about how he could defend himself.
通过我和其他人所做的工作，我们团结了50个国家来支持乌克兰的正义防卫。

955
01:05:33,002 --> 01:05:37,265
Days later, I went to NATO's eastern flank, to Poland and Romania.
正因为我们的支持，提供了空中防御、弹药、火炮、标枪导弹和艾布拉姆斯坦克，乌克兰才能作为一个独立和自由的国家屹立。

956
01:05:38,086 --> 01:05:45,572
And through the work that I and others did, we brought 50 countries together to support Ukraine in its righteous defense.
如果唐纳德·特朗普是总统，普京现在会坐在基辅。

957
01:05:46,232 --> 01:05:59,425
And because of our support, because of the air defense, the ammunition, the artillery, the Javelins, the Abrams tanks that we have provided, Ukraine stands as an independent and free country.
要理解这将意味着什么，因为普京的议程不仅仅关乎乌克兰。

958
01:05:59,665 --> 01:06:03,128
If Donald Trump were president, Putin would be sitting in Kiev right now.
要理解为什么我们的欧洲盟友和北约盟友如此感激您不再是总统，我们理解世界上最大的军事联盟——北约的重要性。

959
01:06:03,869 --> 01:06:09,332
And understand what that would mean, because Putin's agenda is not just about Ukraine.
以及我们所做的事情，以维护泽连斯基和乌克兰人民为独立而战的能力。

960
01:06:10,132 --> 01:06:24,380
Understand why the European allies and our NATO allies are so thankful that you are no longer president, and that we understand the importance of the greatest military alliance the world has ever known, which is NATO.
否则，普京将坐在基辅，目光瞄准欧洲其他地区，首先是波兰。

961
01:06:25,200 --> 01:06:31,964
and what we have done to preserve the ability of Zelensky and the Ukrainians to fight for their independence.
并且我们所做的一切都是为了维护乌克兰的独立。

962
01:06:32,425 --> 01:06:38,728
Otherwise, Putin would be sitting in Kiev with his eyes on the rest of Europe, starting with Poland.
我们绝不能让历史重演。

963
01:06:38,788 --> 01:06:53,618
And why don't you tell the 800,000 Polish-Americans right here in Pennsylvania how quickly you would give up for the sake of favor and what you think is a friendship with what is known to be a dictator who would eat you for lunch.
你为什么不告诉在宾夕法尼亚州的80万波兰裔美国人，你会多快为了所谓的友谊而放弃一切，以及你认为与众所周知的会把你吞掉的独裁者的关系呢？

964
01:06:55,182 --> 01:06:56,283
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢您。

965
01:06:56,303 --> 01:06:58,083
We've heard from both of you on Ukraine tonight.
今晚我们听到了你们双方对乌克兰的看法。

966
01:06:58,284 --> 01:06:59,984
Afghanistan came up in the last hour.
阿富汗在过去一个小时中被提及。

967
01:07:00,004 --> 01:07:02,546
I wanted her to respond to something you said earlier.
我想让她回应你之前说的某些话。

968
01:07:03,586 --> 01:07:05,007
Please, I'll give you a minute here.
请，你有一分钟的时间。

969
01:07:06,229 --> 01:07:13,813
Putin would be sitting in Moscow, and he wouldn't have lost 300,000 men and women, but he would have been sitting in Moscow.
普京会坐在莫斯科，他不会失去30万名男女，但他会坐在莫斯科。

970
01:07:14,254 --> 01:07:14,954
Quiet, please.
请安静。

971
01:07:15,554 --> 01:07:19,997
He would have been sitting in Moscow much happier than he is right now.
他会比现在更快乐地坐在莫斯科。

972
01:07:20,717 --> 01:07:23,939
But eventually, you know, he's got a thing that other people don't have.
但最终，你知道，他有一些其他人没有的东西。

973
01:07:23,959 --> 01:07:24,980
He's got nuclear weapons.
他拥有核武器。

974
01:07:25,000 --> 01:07:26,160
They don't ever talk about that.
他们从来不谈论这个。

975
01:07:26,180 --> 01:07:27,321
He's got nuclear weapons.
他拥有核武器。

976
01:07:27,741 --> 01:07:28,922
Nobody ever thinks about that.
没有人会想到这一点。

977
01:07:29,522 --> 01:07:33,945
And eventually, maybe he'll use them, and maybe he hasn't been that threatening.
最终，也许他会使用它，也许他并没有那么具威胁性。

978
01:07:34,545 --> 01:07:37,966
But he does have that, something we don't even like to talk about.
但他确实拥有这个，我们甚至不喜欢谈论。

979
01:07:38,147 --> 01:07:39,447
Nobody likes to talk about it.
没有人喜欢谈论这个。

980
01:07:39,867 --> 01:07:44,829
But just so you understand, they sent her to negotiate peace before this war started.
但让你明白的是，在这场战争开始之前，他们派她去谈判和平。

981
01:07:45,209 --> 01:07:51,792
Three days later, he went in and he started the war because everything they said was weak and stupid.
三天后，他入侵并开始了战争，因为他们所说的一切都是软弱而愚蠢的。

982
01:07:52,112 --> 01:07:53,373
They said the wrong things.
他们说错了话。

983
01:07:53,613 --> 01:07:55,173
That war should have never started.
这场战争根本不应该开始。

984
01:07:55,494 --> 01:07:56,674
She was the emissary.
她是特使。

985
01:07:56,974 --> 01:08:00,936
They sent her in to negotiate with Zelensky and Putin.
他们派她去与泽连斯基和普京谈判。

986
01:08:01,636 --> 01:08:02,276
And she did.
她确实去了。

987
01:08:02,717 --> 01:08:04,398
And the war started three days later.
而战争在三天后开始。

988
01:08:04,778 --> 01:08:06,919
And that's the kind of talent we have with her.
这就是我们与她的才华。

989
01:08:07,259 --> 01:08:09,241
She's worse than Biden, in my opinion.
在我看来，她比拜登更糟糕。

990
01:08:09,281 --> 01:08:11,642
I think he's the worst president in the history of our country.
我认为他是我们国家历史上最糟糕的总统。

991
01:08:12,022 --> 01:08:15,685
She goes down as the worst vice president in the history of our country.
她将被记住为我们国家历史上最糟糕的副总统。

992
01:08:15,725 --> 01:08:16,745
But let me tell you something.
但让我告诉你一些事情。

993
01:08:17,225 --> 01:08:19,427
She is a horrible negotiator.
她是一个糟糕的谈判者。

994
01:08:19,927 --> 01:08:21,608
They sent her in to negotiate.
他们派她去谈判。

995
01:08:21,868 --> 01:08:24,550
As soon as they left, Putin did the invasion.
一离开，普京就入侵了。

996
01:08:24,790 --> 01:08:25,571
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢您。

997
01:08:25,591 --> 01:08:26,392
You did bring up something.
您确实提到了一些事情。

998
01:08:26,512 --> 01:08:28,354
You said she went to negotiate with Vladimir Putin.
您说她去和弗拉基米尔·普京谈判。

999
01:08:28,374 --> 01:08:30,637
Vice President Harris, have you ever met Vladimir Putin?
哈里斯副总统，您见过弗拉基米尔·普京吗？

1000
01:08:30,657 --> 01:08:31,619
Can you clarify tonight?
今晚能澄清一下吗？

1001
01:08:32,359 --> 01:08:35,984
Yet again, I said at the beginning of this debate, you're going to hear a bunch of lies coming from this fellow.
我在本次辩论开始时就说过，您将听到这个家伙说的一堆谎言。

1002
01:08:36,525 --> 01:08:37,326
And that is another one.
这又是其中之一。

1003
01:08:38,287 --> 01:08:42,052
When I went to meet with President Zelensky, I've now met with him over five times.
当我去见泽伦斯基总统时，我已经见过他超过五次。

1004
01:08:43,345 --> 01:09:05,650
The reality is it has been about standing as America always should, as a leader upholding international rules and norms, as a leader who shows strength, understanding that the alliances we have around the world are dependent on our ability to look out for our friends and not favor
现实是，作为美国，我们应该始终站出来，作为维护国际规则和规范的领导者，作为展现力量的领导者，理解我们在全球的联盟依赖于我们照顾朋友的能力，而不是偏袒

1005
01:09:06,050 --> 01:09:11,914
our enemies because you adore strongmen instead of caring about democracy.
我们的敌人，因为您崇拜强人而不在乎民主。

1006
01:09:12,475 --> 01:09:15,157
And that is very much what is at stake here.
这正是这里面所涉及的重大问题。

1007
01:09:15,377 --> 01:09:21,981
The president of the United States is commander in chief, and the American people have a right to rely
美国总统是最高统帅，美国人民有权依赖

1008
01:09:22,962 --> 01:09:40,143
on a president who understands the significance of America's role and responsibility in terms of ensuring that there is stability and ensuring we stand up for our principles and not sell them for the benefit of personal flattery.
一位理解美国角色和责任重要性的总统，以确保稳定，并确保我们坚守原则，而不是为了个人的奉承而出卖这些原则。

1009
01:09:40,711 --> 01:09:42,712
We've talked about Ukraine and Vladimir Putin.
我们谈论过乌克兰和弗拉基米尔·普京。

1010
01:09:42,772 --> 01:09:44,173
I do want to talk about Afghanistan.
我确实想谈谈阿富汗。

1011
01:09:44,213 --> 01:09:46,435
It came up in the first hour of this debate.
在本次辩论的第一小时中提到过。

1012
01:09:47,376 --> 01:09:48,737
I want to move on to Afghanistan.
我想继续谈阿富汗。

1013
01:09:49,397 --> 01:09:51,819
Trump did the most amazing thing I've ever seen.
特朗普做了我见过的最惊人的事情。

1014
01:09:52,199 --> 01:09:56,502
He got these countries, the 28 countries at the time, to pay up.
他让这28个国家支付了费用。

1015
01:09:56,682 --> 01:09:57,783
He said, I've never seen.
他说，我从未见过。

1016
01:09:57,843 --> 01:09:58,844
He's the head of NATO.
他是北约的首脑。

1017
01:09:59,204 --> 01:10:00,365
He said, I've never seen.
他说，我从未见过。

1018
01:10:00,625 --> 01:10:03,287
For years, we were paying almost all of NATO.
多年来，我们几乎在为北约支付全部费用。

1019
01:10:03,647 --> 01:10:07,828
We were being ripped off by European nations, both on trade and on NATO.
我们在贸易和北约上被欧洲国家剥削。

1020
01:10:08,428 --> 01:10:14,630
I got them to pay up by saying one of the statements you made before, if you don't pay, we're not going to protect you.
我通过引用你之前说过的一句话让他们支付，如果你们不付款，我们就不会保护你。

1021
01:10:14,690 --> 01:10:15,971
Otherwise, we would have never gotten it.
否则，我们根本不会得到这些。

1022
01:10:16,251 --> 01:10:19,972
He said it was one of the most incredible jobs that he's ever seen done.
他说这是他见过的最不可思议的工作之一。

1023
01:10:20,072 --> 01:10:20,412
Thank you.
谢谢。

1024
01:10:20,652 --> 01:10:21,813
I want to turn to Afghanistan.
我想谈谈阿富汗。

1025
01:10:21,953 --> 01:10:29,778
It came up in the first hour of the debate, and we witnessed a poignant moment today on Capitol Hill honoring the soldiers who died in the chaotic withdrawal from Afghanistan.
在辩论的第一个小时中提到了这一点，今天我们在国会山见证了一个动人的时刻，纪念在阿富汗混乱撤退中牺牲的士兵。

1026
01:10:29,859 --> 01:10:35,863
I do want to ask the vice president, do you believe you bear any responsibility in the way that withdrawal played out?
我确实想问副总统，您认为您对撤军的方式有责任吗？

1027
01:10:37,113 --> 01:10:41,798
Well, I will tell you, I agreed with President Biden's decision to pull out of Afghanistan.
好吧，我告诉你，我同意拜登总统撤出阿富汗的决定。

1028
01:10:42,439 --> 01:10:45,502
Four presidents said they would, and Joe Biden did.
四位总统曾表示他们会这样做，而乔·拜登做到了。

1029
01:10:46,443 --> 01:10:53,210
And as a result, America's taxpayers are not paying the $300 million a day we were paying for that endless war.
因此，美国纳税人不再支付每天三亿美金用于这场无尽的战争。

1030
01:10:54,131 --> 01:11:05,859
And as of today, there is not one member of the United States military who is in active duty in a combat zone in any war zone around the world the first time this century.
截至今天，美国军队中没有一名成员在全球任何战区处于战斗状态，这是本世纪第一次。

1031
01:11:06,439 --> 01:11:09,501
But let's understand how we got to where we are.
但我们要理解我们是如何走到今天这一步的。

1032
01:11:10,022 --> 01:11:15,806
Donald Trump, when he was president, negotiated one of the weakest deals you can imagine.
唐纳德·特朗普在担任总统时，谈判了一份你能想象的最弱的协议。

1033
01:11:15,846 --> 01:11:17,467
He calls himself a dealmaker.
他自称是个交易者。

1034
01:11:17,887 --> 01:11:22,270
Even his national security adviser said it was a weak, terrible deal.
甚至他的国家安全顾问也说这是一个弱而糟糕的协议。

1035
01:11:22,330 --> 01:11:23,491
And here's how it went down.
事情就是这样发生的。

1036
01:11:24,331 --> 01:11:26,473
He bypassed the Afghan government.
他绕过了阿富汗政府。

1037
01:11:27,114 --> 01:11:31,118
He negotiated directly with a terrorist organization called the Taliban.
他直接与一个叫塔利班的恐怖组织进行谈判。

1038
01:11:31,778 --> 01:11:37,644
The negotiation involved the Taliban getting 5,000 terrorists, Taliban terrorists, released.
谈判内容包括释放5000名塔利班恐怖分子。

1039
01:11:37,944 --> 01:11:45,511
And get this, no get this, and the president at the time invited the Taliban to Camp David.
你听好，没错，时任总统邀请塔利班到戴维营。

1040
01:11:46,681 --> 01:12:00,235
a place of storied significance for us as Americans, a place where we honor the importance of American diplomacy, where we invite and receive respected world leaders, and this
这是一个对我们作为美国人具有重要意义的地方，一个我们尊重美国外交重要性的地方，在这里我们邀请并接待受人尊敬的世界领导人，而这……

1041
01:12:03,055 --> 01:12:20,707
former President, as President, invited them to Camp David because he does not, again, appreciate the role and responsibility of the President of the United States to be Commander-in-Chief with a level of respect.
前总统作为总统邀请他们去戴维营，因为他再次不理解美国总统作为总司令的角色和责任。

1042
01:12:21,087 --> 01:12:32,735
And this gets back to the point of how he has consistently disparaged and demeaned members of our military, fallen soldiers, and the work that we must do to uphold the strength
这又回到了他如何持续贬低和侮辱我们军队成员、阵亡士兵，以及我们必须做的工作，以维护美国在全球的力量和尊重的问题。

1043
01:12:33,295 --> 01:12:36,817
and the respect of the United States of America around the world.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢您。

1044
01:12:36,857 --> 01:12:38,018
Vice President Harris, thank you.
特朗普总统，您对此她说您开始与塔利班谈判的回应是什么？

1045
01:12:38,078 --> 01:12:41,620
President Trump, your response to her saying that you began the negotiations with the Taliban?
如果你看看那个时期，塔利班正在用狙击枪杀害我们的士兵，很多士兵。

1046
01:12:43,317 --> 01:12:50,838
If you take a look at that period of time, the Taliban was killing our soldiers, a lot of them, with snipers.
我参与塔利班的原因是因为塔利班在进行杀戮。

1047
01:12:51,979 --> 01:12:56,460
And I got involved with the Taliban because the Taliban was doing the killing.
那是阿富汗的战斗力量。

1048
01:12:56,560 --> 01:12:58,680
That's the fighting force within Afghanistan.
他们不愿意这样做，因为你知道，他们总是与错误的人打交道。

1049
01:12:58,700 --> 01:13:01,661
They don't bother doing that because, you know, they deal with the wrong people all the time.
但我参与了。

1050
01:13:02,221 --> 01:13:03,381
But I got involved.
阿卜杜勒是塔利班的头目。

1051
01:13:04,121 --> 01:13:06,922
And Abdul is the head of the Taliban.
他仍然是塔利班的头目。

1052
01:13:06,962 --> 01:13:08,582
He is still the head of the Taliban.
我告诉阿卜杜勒，不要再这样做了。

1053
01:13:09,042 --> 01:13:11,103
And I told Abdul, don't do it anymore.
如果你再这样做，你会有麻烦。

1054
01:13:11,163 --> 01:13:13,063
You do it anymore, you're going to have problems.
他说，为什么你给我发我房子的照片？

1055
01:13:13,563 --> 01:13:15,784
And he said, why do you send me a picture of my house?
我说，你得自己想办法，阿卜杜勒。

1056
01:13:15,844 --> 01:13:17,845
I said, you're going to have to figure that out, Abdul.
在18个月内，我们没有人被杀。

1057
01:13:18,285 --> 01:13:21,125
And for 18 months, we had nobody killed.
我们确实有一个由迈克·蓬佩奥谈判的协议。

1058
01:13:21,546 --> 01:13:24,146
We did have an agreement negotiated by Mike Pompeo.
这是一个非常好的协议。

1059
01:13:24,546 --> 01:13:25,567
It was a very good agreement.
之所以好，是因为我们要撤出。

1060
01:13:25,887 --> 01:13:29,148
The reason it was good, it was we were getting out.
我们本可以比他们更快撤出，但我们不会失去士兵。

1061
01:13:29,268 --> 01:13:32,029
We would have been out faster than them, but we wouldn't have lost the soldiers.
我们不会留下很多美国人。

1062
01:13:32,309 --> 01:13:34,429
We wouldn't have left many Americans behind.
我们不会留下。

1063
01:13:34,629 --> 01:13:35,329
We wouldn't have left.
我们不会留下。

1064
01:13:35,730 --> 01:13:36,410
We wouldn't have left.
价值850亿美元的全新美丽军事装备也没有留下，最后他们破坏了协议，协议说你必须做到这个这个这个这个这个，但他们没有做到，他们没有做到，

1065
01:13:38,111 --> 01:13:52,844
$85 billion worth of brand-new beautiful military equipment behind and just to finish they Blew it the agreement said you have to do this this this this this and they didn't do it They didn't do it the agreement was
协议因他们没有履行应有的义务而被我们终止。

1066
01:13:53,544 --> 01:13:58,769
was terminated by us because they didn't do what they were supposed to do.
[Translation missing line - 26]

1067
01:13:59,409 --> 01:14:06,415
And these people did the worst withdrawal and, in my opinion, the most embarrassing moment in the history of our country.
在我看来，这些人进行了最糟糕的撤军，这是我们国家历史上最尴尬的时刻。

1068
01:14:06,716 --> 01:14:13,562
And by the way, that's why Russia attacked Ukraine, because they saw how incompetent she and her boss are.
顺便说一下，这就是为什么俄罗斯攻击乌克兰，因为他们看到了她和她的老板是多么无能。

1069
01:14:13,942 --> 01:14:14,822
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢您。

1070
01:14:15,803 --> 01:14:18,164
I want to move on now to race and politics in this country.
我现在想谈谈这个国家的种族与政治。

1071
01:14:18,384 --> 01:14:27,367
Mr. President, you recently said of Vice President Harris, quote, I didn't know she was black until a number of years ago when she happened to turn black and now she wants to be known as black.
总统先生，您最近提到副总统哈里斯时说：“我不知道她是黑人，直到几年前，她突然变成黑人，现在她想被称为黑人。”

1072
01:14:28,028 --> 01:14:29,948
I want to ask a bigger picture question here tonight.
我想今晚问一个更大的问题。

1073
01:14:30,589 --> 01:14:34,630
Why do you believe it's appropriate to weigh in on the racial identity of your opponent?
您认为为什么有必要对您对手的种族身份发表看法？

1074
01:14:34,830 --> 01:14:35,871
I don't and I don't care.
我不这样认为，我也不在乎。

1075
01:14:35,891 --> 01:14:37,391
I don't care what she is.
我不在乎她是什么。

1076
01:14:37,892 --> 01:14:38,272
I don't care.
我不在乎。

1077
01:14:39,267 --> 01:14:42,309
uh, you make a big deal out of something, I couldn't care less.
呃，您把一件事搞得很严重，我根本不在乎。

1078
01:14:43,029 --> 01:14:44,810
Whatever she wants to be is okay with me.
她想成为什么都可以。

1079
01:14:45,410 --> 01:14:46,351
But those were your words.
但那是您的话。

1080
01:14:46,371 --> 01:14:46,931
So I don't know.
所以我不知道。

1081
01:14:47,131 --> 01:14:47,451
I don't know.
我不知道。

1082
01:14:47,471 --> 01:14:54,695
I mean, all I can say is I read where she was not black that she put out and I'll say that.
我的意思是，我只能说我看到她曾说过自己不是黑人，我会这么说。

1083
01:14:55,055 --> 01:14:58,157
And then I read that she was black and that's okay.
然后我看到她说自己是黑人，这没问题。

1084
01:14:58,297 --> 01:14:59,538
Either one was okay with me.
无论哪种说法我都可以接受。

1085
01:14:59,798 --> 01:15:00,518
That's up to her.
这取决于她。

1086
01:15:00,959 --> 01:15:01,559
That's up to her.
这取决于她。

1087
01:15:01,859 --> 01:15:03,200
Vice President Harris, your thoughts on this?
哈里斯副总统，您对此有何看法？

1088
01:15:05,114 --> 01:15:19,784
I think it's – I mean, honestly, I think it's a tragedy that we have someone who wants to be president who has consistently over the course of his career attempted to use race to divide the American people.
我认为这是一场悲剧，真的，我认为有一个人想当总统，却在他的职业生涯中不断试图利用种族来分裂美国人民。

1089
01:15:20,814 --> 01:15:32,117
You know, I do believe that the vast majority of us know that we have so much more in common than what separates us, and we don't want this kind of approach that is just constantly trying to divide us, and especially by race.
你知道，我确实相信我们绝大多数人都知道，我们有更多共同点，而不是分隔我们的东西，我们不想要这种不断试图通过种族来分裂我们的方式。

1090
01:15:32,197 --> 01:15:35,258
And let's remember how Donald Trump started.
让我们回想一下唐纳德·特朗普是如何开始的。

1091
01:15:35,378 --> 01:15:46,442
He was a land—he owned land, he owned buildings, and he was investigated because he refused to rent.
他拥有土地，他拥有建筑，因拒绝将房产出租给黑人家庭而受到调查。

1092
01:15:47,639 --> 01:15:49,100
property to black families.
这让他受到了调查。

1093
01:15:49,921 --> 01:16:05,812
Let's remember, this is the same individual who took out a full page ad in the New York Times calling for the execution of five young black and Latino boys who were innocent, the Central Park Five.
让我们记住，这就是那个在《纽约时报》上刊登整版广告，呼吁处决五名无辜的年轻黑人和拉丁裔男孩的个人，中央公园五人组。

1094
01:16:07,659 --> 01:16:10,700
took out a full-page ad calling for their execution.
刊登整版广告，呼吁处决他们。

1095
01:16:11,020 --> 01:16:17,763
This is the same individual who spread birther lies about the first black president of the United States.
这个人曾散布关于美国第一位黑人总统的诽谤谎言。

1096
01:16:19,043 --> 01:16:29,207
And I think the American people want better than that, want better than this, want someone who understands, as I do, I travel our country.
我认为美国人民想要更好的领导，想要更美好的未来，想要一个像我一样理解他们的人，我走遍了我们的国家。

1097
01:16:30,580 --> 01:16:33,222
We see in each other a friend.
我们彼此之间看到的是朋友。

1098
01:16:33,382 --> 01:16:35,363
We see in each other a neighbor.
我们彼此之间看到的是邻居。

1099
01:16:36,024 --> 01:16:42,629
We don't want a leader who is constantly trying to have Americans point their fingers at each other.
我们不想要一个不断试图让美国人互相指责的领导者。

1100
01:16:43,529 --> 01:16:46,471
I meet with people all the time who tell me
我经常与人们会面，他们告诉我

1101
01:16:47,612 --> 01:16:55,894
Can we please just have discourse about how we're going to invest in the aspirations and the ambitions and the dreams of the American people?
我们能不能就如何投资于美国人民的愿望、抱负和梦想进行讨论？

1102
01:16:56,714 --> 01:17:08,598
Knowing that regardless of people's color or the language their grandmother speaks, we all have the same dreams and aspirations and want a president who invests in those, not in hate and division.
无论人们的肤色或他们祖母说的语言是什么，我们都有着相同的梦想和抱负，想要一个投资于这些，而不是仇恨和分裂的总统。

1103
01:17:09,238 --> 01:17:10,378
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢您。

1104
01:17:10,538 --> 01:17:10,858
Lindsey?
林赛？

1105
01:17:11,078 --> 01:17:12,919
President Trump, this is now your third time
特朗普总统，这是您第三次

1106
01:17:14,545 --> 01:17:19,326
This is the most divisive presidency in the history of our country.
这是我们国家历史上最具分裂性的总统任期。

1107
01:17:19,606 --> 01:17:20,987
There's never been anything like it.
从未有过这样的情况。

1108
01:17:21,207 --> 01:17:26,848
They're destroying our country, and they come up with things like what she just said.
他们正在摧毁我们的国家，而他们提出的事情就像她刚才所说的那样。

1109
01:17:27,649 --> 01:17:35,831
Going back many, many years, when a lot of people, including Mayor Bloomberg, agreed with me on the Central Park Five, they admitted, they said, they pled guilty.
回到许多年前，当时很多人，包括布隆伯格市长，都同意我对中央公园五人组的看法，他们承认，他们说，他们认罪了。

1110
01:17:37,096 --> 01:17:41,818
And I said, well, if they pled guilty, they'd badly hurt a person, killed a person, ultimately.
我说，如果他们认罪，伤害了一个人，最终杀了一个人。

1111
01:17:42,539 --> 01:17:44,199
And if they pled guilty, then they pled.
如果他们认罪，那就认罪了。

1112
01:17:44,459 --> 01:17:45,120
We're not guilty.
我们无罪。

1113
01:17:45,760 --> 01:17:53,143
But this is a person that has to stretch back years, 40, 50 years ago, because there's nothing now.
但这个人必须追溯到40、50年前，因为现在没有任何事情。

1114
01:17:53,424 --> 01:17:58,306
I built one of the greatest economies in the history of the world, and I'm going to build it again.
我建立了历史上最伟大的经济之一，我会再建立一次。

1115
01:17:58,446 --> 01:18:00,247
It's going to be bigger, better and stronger.
它会更大、更好、更强。

1116
01:18:01,027 --> 01:18:02,587
But they're destroying our economy.
但他们正在摧毁我们的经济。

1117
01:18:02,727 --> 01:18:04,848
They have no idea what a good economy is.
他们根本不知道什么是好的经济。

1118
01:18:05,428 --> 01:18:08,089
Their oil policies, every single policy.
他们的石油政策，每一项政策。

1119
01:18:08,409 --> 01:18:09,149
And remember this.
记住这一点

1120
01:18:10,249 --> 01:18:10,990
She is Biden.
她就是拜登

1121
01:18:11,270 --> 01:18:12,890
You know, she's trying to get away from Biden.
你知道，她试图与拜登撇清关系

1122
01:18:12,930 --> 01:18:14,310
I don't know the gentleman, she says.
她说，我不认识那位绅士

1123
01:18:14,911 --> 01:18:15,711
She is Biden.
她就是拜登

1124
01:18:16,251 --> 01:18:18,591
The worst inflation we've ever had.
我们经历过的最糟糕的通货膨胀

1125
01:18:19,232 --> 01:18:22,893
A horrible economy because inflation has made it so bad.
因为通货膨胀让经济变得如此糟糕

1126
01:18:23,833 --> 01:18:25,053
And she can't get away with that.
她无法逃避这一点

1127
01:18:25,093 --> 01:18:25,373
Thank you.
谢谢

1128
01:18:25,393 --> 01:18:25,833
Your time is up.
你的时间已经到了

1129
01:18:25,853 --> 01:18:27,154
I want to respond to that, though.
不过，我想对此做出回应

1130
01:18:27,174 --> 01:18:28,554
I want to just respond briefly.
我想简要回应一下

1131
01:18:29,824 --> 01:18:34,787
Clearly, I am not Joe Biden, and I am certainly not Donald Trump.
显然，我不是乔·拜登，我也绝对不是唐纳德·特朗普

1132
01:18:35,647 --> 01:18:51,417
And what I do offer is a new generation of leadership for our country, one who believes in what is possible, one who brings a sense of optimism about what we can do instead of always disparaging the American people.
我所提供的是一代新的领导，   相信我们能够实现的可能性，   带来一种对我们能做的事情的乐观态度，而不是不断贬低美国人民

1133
01:18:52,237 --> 01:18:54,058
I believe in what we can do to
我相信我们可以

1134
01:18:55,379 --> 01:18:58,763
to strengthen our small businesses, which is why I have a plan.
增强我们的中产阶级和小企业，这就是我有计划的原因

1135
01:18:58,803 --> 01:19:03,327
Let's talk about our plans and let's compare the plans.
让我们谈谈我们的计划，并进行比较

1136
01:19:03,888 --> 01:19:08,253
I have a plan to give startup businesses $50,000 tax deduction
我有一个计划，为初创企业提供50,000美元的税收减免

1137
01:19:10,635 --> 01:19:15,858
to pursue their ambitions, their innovation, their ideas, their hard work.
以追求他们的雄心、创新、想法和辛勤工作

1138
01:19:16,098 --> 01:19:26,062
I have a plan, $6,000 for young families for the first year of your child's life to help you in that most critical stage of your child's development.
我有一个计划，为年轻家庭提供6,000美元   用于你孩子生命的第一年，以帮助你度过孩子成长中最关键的阶段

1139
01:19:26,262 --> 01:19:27,123
I have a plan.
我有一个计划

1140
01:19:27,763 --> 01:19:41,516
That is about allowing people to be able to pursue what has been fleeting in terms of the American dream by offering a help with down payment of $25,000 down payment assistance for first-time home buyers.
这是关于让人们能够追求美国梦中曾经短暂的东西，   通过为首次购房者提供25,000美元的首付援助

1141
01:19:42,076 --> 01:19:52,605
That's the kind of conversation, I believe, David, that people really want tonight, as opposed to a conversation that is constantly about belittling and name-calling.
我相信，戴维，这就是人们今晚真正想要的对话，而不是不断贬低和辱骂的对话

1142
01:19:53,346 --> 01:19:55,188
Let's turn the page and move forward.
让我们翻开新的一页，向前迈进

1143
01:19:55,208 --> 01:19:56,129
President Trump, we have to move on.
特朗普总统，我们必须继续前进

1144
01:19:56,189 --> 01:19:57,290
She has a plan to defund the police.
她有一个计划要削减警察经费

1145
01:19:57,310 --> 01:19:58,971
She has a plan to confiscate everybody's gun.
她有一个计划要没收每个人的枪支

1146
01:19:59,011 --> 01:20:01,394
President Trump, we do have to move on to other issues.
特朗普总统，我们确实需要转到其他议题上

1147
01:20:10,542 --> 01:20:12,603
in Pennsylvania or anywhere else.
在宾夕法尼亚州或其他地方

1148
01:20:12,623 --> 01:20:15,184
That's what her plan is until just recently.
这就是她的计划，直到最近

1149
01:20:15,445 --> 01:20:20,147
The former president has said something twice that I need to respond to.
前总统提到的内容我需要回应两次

1150
01:20:20,187 --> 01:20:23,028
I just need to respond one time to what he has said multiple times.
我只需回应他多次提到的内容一次

1151
01:20:23,049 --> 01:20:26,190
President Trump, this is now your third time running for president.
特朗普总统，这是您第三次竞选总统

1152
01:20:26,250 --> 01:20:31,413
You have long vowed to repeal and replace the Affordable Care Act, also known as Obamacare.
您早已发誓要废除和取代《平价医疗法案》，也就是奥巴马医改

1153
01:20:31,433 --> 01:20:32,854
You have failed to accomplish that.
您未能实现这一承诺

1154
01:20:33,194 --> 01:20:37,436
You now say you're going to keep Obamacare, quote, unless we can do something much better.
您现在说您会保留奥巴马医改，引用，除非我们能做得更好

1155
01:20:37,936 --> 01:20:40,097
Last month, you said, quote, we're working on it.
上个月，您说，引用，我们正在努力

1156
01:20:40,417 --> 01:20:46,199
So tonight, nine years after you first started running, do you have a plan and can you tell us what it is?
所以今晚，在您第一次开始竞选九年后，您有计划吗？您能告诉我们是什么吗？

1157
01:20:46,319 --> 01:20:49,260
Obamacare was lousy health care, always was.
奥巴马医改是一项糟糕的医疗保健，一直都是

1158
01:20:49,640 --> 01:20:50,780
It's not very good today.
今天也不是很好

1159
01:20:51,481 --> 01:20:56,982
And what I said, that if we come up with something and we are working on things, we're going to do it and we're going to replace it.
我说过，如果我们想出一些东西，我们正在努力，

1160
01:20:57,042 --> 01:20:58,063
But remember this.
我们将做到并进行替换

1161
01:20:58,823 --> 01:21:02,665
I inherited Obamacare because Democrats wouldn't change it.
但请记住这一点

1162
01:21:02,705 --> 01:21:03,625
They wouldn't vote for it.
我继承了奥巴马医改，因为民主党人不愿改变它

1163
01:21:03,985 --> 01:21:04,825
They were unanimous.
他们不会投票支持

1164
01:21:04,865 --> 01:21:06,306
They wouldn't vote to change it.
他们是一致反对

1165
01:21:06,686 --> 01:21:10,307
If they would have done that, we would have had a much better plan than Obamacare.
他们不会投票改变它

1166
01:21:10,668 --> 01:21:13,469
But the Democrats came up, they wouldn't vote for it.
如果他们愿意这样做，我们将拥有比奥巴马医改更好的计划

1167
01:21:13,969 --> 01:21:15,870
I had a choice to make when I was president.
但民主党人提出了，他们不会投票支持

1168
01:21:16,190 --> 01:21:21,792
Do I save it and make it as good as it can be, never going to be great, or do I let it rot?
作为总统，我面临选择

1169
01:21:22,492 --> 01:21:28,155
And I felt I had an obligation, even though politically it would have been good to just let it rot and let it go away.
我是否要拯救它并尽可能使其变好，永远不会变得伟大，还是让我它腐烂？

1170
01:21:28,795 --> 01:21:32,377
I decided, and I told my people, the top people, and they're very good people.
我觉得我有责任，尽管从政治上讲，简单地让它腐烂让它消失是好的选择

1171
01:21:32,397 --> 01:21:34,838
I have a lot of good people in this, that administration.
我在这个政府里有很多优秀的人。

1172
01:21:35,398 --> 01:21:36,439
We read about the bad ones.
我们听说了坏的。

1173
01:21:36,459 --> 01:21:38,640
We had some real bad ones too, and so do they.
我们也有一些真正糟糕的人，他们也有。

1174
01:21:38,680 --> 01:21:39,680
They have really bad ones.
他们有非常糟糕的人。

1175
01:21:39,700 --> 01:21:40,921
The difference is they don't get rid of them.
区别在于他们不把这些人处理掉。

1176
01:21:40,941 --> 01:21:41,461
But let me just
但让我来解释一下。

1177
01:21:41,741 --> 01:21:42,141
explain.
我有一个选择。

1178
01:21:42,762 --> 01:21:43,922
I had a choice to make.
我是否要拯救它并让它尽可能地好？

1179
01:21:44,302 --> 01:21:47,104
Do I save it and make it as good as it can be?
还是让我让它腐烂？

1180
01:21:47,504 --> 01:21:48,465
Or do I let it rot?
我拯救了它。

1181
01:21:49,005 --> 01:21:49,825
And I saved it.
我做了正确的事。

1182
01:21:49,985 --> 01:21:51,026
I did the right thing.
但它永远不会变得伟大，而且对人们来说太贵了。

1183
01:21:51,466 --> 01:21:55,768
But it's still never going to be great, and it's too expensive for people.
我们要做的是研究不同的计划。

1184
01:21:56,289 --> 01:21:59,390
And what we will do is we're looking at different plans.
如果我们能想出一个能让

1185
01:21:59,791 --> 01:22:01,972
If we can come up with a plan that's going to cost
我们的人民，居民，花费更少的钱，并且比平价医疗法案更好的医疗保健计划，那么我绝对会这样做。

1186
01:22:02,552 --> 01:22:09,758
our people, our population, less money, and be better healthcare than Obamacare, then I would absolutely do it.
但在那之前，我会尽可能好地运营它。

1187
01:22:10,158 --> 01:22:13,061
But until then, I'd run it as good as it can be run.
所以，简单地说，是或不是，你仍然没有计划？

1188
01:22:13,341 --> 01:22:15,463
So, just a yes or no, you still do not have a plan?
我有一个计划的概念。

1189
01:22:15,863 --> 01:22:17,324
I have concepts of a plan.
我现在不是总统。

1190
01:22:17,985 --> 01:22:19,366
I'm not president right now.
但如果

1191
01:22:19,806 --> 01:22:20,306
But if
我们想出一些东西。

1192
01:22:21,604 --> 01:22:22,845
We come up with something.
只有在我们想出更好且更便宜的方案时，我才会进行更改。

1193
01:22:22,865 --> 01:22:26,748
I would only change it if we come up with something that's better and less expensive.
我们有一些概念和选项可以做到这一点。

1194
01:22:27,108 --> 01:22:31,192
And there are concepts and options we have to do that.
你将在不久的将来听到有关它的消息。

1195
01:22:31,512 --> 01:22:34,114
And you'll be hearing about it in the not-too-distant future.
哈里斯副总统，在2017年，你支持伯尼·桑德斯的提案，取消私人保险，建立一个政府运营的医疗保健系统。

1196
01:22:34,354 --> 01:22:41,620
Vice President Harris, in 2017, you supported Bernie Sanders' proposal to do away with private insurance and create a government-run healthcare system.
这将是一个全新的医疗保健系统。

1197
01:22:42,041 --> 01:22:45,944
Two years later, you proposed a plan that included a private insurance option.
两年后，你提出了一个包括私人保险选项的计划。

1198
01:22:46,264 --> 01:22:47,185
What is your plan today?
你今天的计划是什么？

1199
01:22:47,745 --> 01:22:56,949
Well, first of all, I absolutely support, and over the last four years as vice president, private healthcare options, but what we need to do is maintain and grow the Affordable Care Act.
首先，我绝对支持，在过去四年担任副总统期间，私人医疗保健选项，但我们需要做的就是维护和发展负担能力法案。

1200
01:22:56,969 --> 01:23:02,371
But I'll get to that, Lindsay, I just need to respond to a previous point that the former president has made.
不过，林赛，我会谈到这一点，我只需要回应前总统提出的一个观点。

1201
01:23:02,691 --> 01:23:07,453
I've made very clear my position on fracking, and then this business about taking everyone's guns away.
我已经明确表明了我对水力压裂的立场，还有关于夺走每个人的枪支这件事。

1202
01:23:08,054 --> 01:23:09,554
Tim Walz and I are both gun owners.
蒂姆·沃兹和我都是持枪者。

1203
01:23:09,594 --> 01:23:13,556
We're not taking anybody's guns away, so stop with the continuous lying about this stuff.
我们不会夺走任何人的枪，所以请停止关于这件事的持续谎言。

1204
01:23:14,614 --> 01:23:19,656
As it relates to the Affordable Care Act, understand, just look at the history to know where people stand.
关于负担能力法案，要理解这一点，只需看看历史，了解人们的立场。

1205
01:23:20,076 --> 01:23:26,298
When Donald Trump was president, 60 times he tried to get rid of the Affordable Care Act.
当唐纳德·特朗普担任总统时，他尝试了60次废除负担能力法案。

1206
01:23:26,318 --> 01:23:26,798
60 times.
60次。

1207
01:23:27,059 --> 01:23:36,302
I was a senator at the time when, I will never forget the early morning hours when it was up for a vote in the United States Senate.
我那时是参议员，我永远不会忘记在美国参议院投票的清晨时光。

1208
01:23:36,762 --> 01:23:41,424
And the late, great John McCain, who you have disparaged,
已故的伟大约翰·麦凯恩，你曾贬低他，

1209
01:23:42,464 --> 01:23:47,928
as being, you don't like him, you said, at the time, because he got caught.
因为你不喜欢他，你曾说过，因为他被抓住了。

1210
01:23:48,028 --> 01:23:49,329
He was an American hero.
他是美国英雄。

1211
01:23:49,589 --> 01:23:56,454
The late, great John McCain, I will never forget that night, walked onto the Senate floor and said, no you don't.
已故的伟大约翰·麦凯恩，我永远不会忘记那晚，他走上参议院的地板说，不，你不能。

1212
01:23:57,154 --> 01:23:57,755
No you don't.
不，你不能。

1213
01:23:58,255 --> 01:24:00,516
No, you don't get rid of the Affordable Care Act.
不，你不能废除负担能力法案。

1214
01:24:00,536 --> 01:24:01,717
You have no plan.
你没有计划。

1215
01:24:02,358 --> 01:24:09,482
And what the Affordable Care Act has done is eliminate the ability of insurance companies to deny people with pre-existing conditions.
负担能力法案所做的就是消除保险公司拒绝有既往病史的人投保的能力。

1216
01:24:09,962 --> 01:24:12,764
I don't have to tell the people watching tonight, you remember what that was like?
我不需要告诉今晚观看的人，你们还记得那是什么样子吗？

1217
01:24:13,664 --> 01:24:16,046
Remember when an insurance company could deny
记得当一家保险公司可以拒绝

1218
01:24:17,176 --> 01:24:23,559
if a child had asthma, if someone was a breast cancer survivor, if a grandparent had diabetes.
一个有哮喘的孩子，一个乳腺癌幸存者，或者一个有糖尿病的祖父母吗？

1219
01:24:24,240 --> 01:24:36,446
And thankfully, as I've been vice president and we over the last four years have strengthened the Affordable Care Act, we have allowed for the first time Medicare to negotiate drug prices on behalf of you, the American people.
感谢上帝，作为副总统，我们在过去四年中加强了负担能力法案，我们首次允许医疗保险代表你们，

1220
01:24:36,787 --> 01:24:39,028
Donald Trump said he was going to allow Medicare to negotiate
美国人民协商药品价格。

1221
01:24:40,068 --> 01:24:40,569
drug prices?
唐纳德·特朗普说他会允许医疗保险协商

1222
01:24:40,609 --> 01:24:41,089
He never did.
药品价格？他从未这样做。

1223
01:24:41,169 --> 01:24:41,490
We did.
我们做到了。

1224
01:24:42,030 --> 01:24:44,933
And now we have capped the cost of insulin at $35 a month.
现在我们将胰岛素的费用限制在每月35美元。

1225
01:24:45,213 --> 01:24:50,538
Since I've been vice president, we have capped the cost of prescription medication for seniors at $2,000 a year.
自我担任副总统以来，我们已将老年人的处方药费用限制在每年2000美元。

1226
01:24:50,938 --> 01:24:57,083
And when I am president, we will do that for all people, understanding that the value I bring to this
当我成为总统时，我们将为所有人做到这一点，因为我认为

1227
01:24:57,944 --> 01:25:04,146
is that access to health care should be a right and not just a privilege of those who can afford it.
医疗保健的获取应当是一项权利，而不仅仅是那些能够负担得起的人的特权。

1228
01:25:04,606 --> 01:25:13,449
And the plan has to be to strengthen the Affordable Care Act, not get rid of it, practice prologue in terms of where Donald Trump stands on that.
我们的计划必须是加强《负担得起的医疗法案》，而不是废除它，了解唐纳德·特朗普在这一点上的立场。

1229
01:25:13,489 --> 01:25:16,470
I want to move to an issue that's important for a lot of... You made a mistake.
我想转到一个对许多人来说很重要的问题……你犯了一个错误。

1230
01:25:17,290 --> 01:25:21,371
At number one, John McCain fought Obamacare for 10 years.
首先，约翰·麦凯恩为奥巴马医改奋斗了10年。

1231
01:25:22,111 --> 01:25:23,272
But it wasn't only him.
但不仅仅是他。

1232
01:25:23,472 --> 01:25:26,433
It were all of the Democrats that kept it going.
所有的民主党人都在支持它。

1233
01:25:26,853 --> 01:25:27,433
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1234
01:25:28,837 --> 01:25:31,619
We can do much better than Obamacare, much less money.
我们可以做得比奥巴马医改更好，花费更少。

1235
01:25:31,979 --> 01:25:37,083
But she won't improve private insurance for people, private medical insurance.
但她不会改善人们的私人保险，私人医疗保险。

1236
01:25:37,784 --> 01:25:39,425
That's another thing she doesn't want to get.
这是她不想得到的另一件事。

1237
01:25:39,445 --> 01:25:45,189
People are paying privately for insurance that have worked hard and made money and they want to have private.
那些努力工作并赚钱的人正在为私人保险付费，他们希望拥有私人保险。

1238
01:25:45,389 --> 01:25:48,812
She wants everybody to be on government insurance where you wait.
她希望每个人都在政府保险下等待。

1239
01:25:49,372 --> 01:25:51,494
Six months for an operation that you need immediately.
等六个月才能进行你急需的手术。

1240
01:25:51,514 --> 01:25:52,675
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢您。

1241
01:25:52,735 --> 01:25:59,060
We have another issue that we'd like to get to that's important for a number of Americans, in particular younger voters, and that's climate change.
我们还有另一个问题，希望能讨论，这对许多美国人，尤其是年轻选民很重要，那就是气候变化。

1242
01:25:59,380 --> 01:26:04,144
President Trump, with regard to the environment, you say that we have to have clean air and clean water.
特朗普总统，关于环境问题，您说我们必须有清洁的空气和清洁的水。

1243
01:26:04,504 --> 01:26:08,207
Vice President Harris, you call climate change an existential threat.
哈里斯副总统，您称气候变化是一个生存威胁。

1244
01:26:08,587 --> 01:26:12,751
The question to you both tonight is what would you do to fight climate change?
今晚的问题是，你们将如何应对气候变化？

1245
01:26:12,871 --> 01:26:14,592
And Vice President Harris, we'll start with you.
哈里斯副总统，我们从您开始。

1246
01:26:14,832 --> 01:26:15,673
One minute for you each.
你们各有一分钟时间。

1247
01:26:16,360 --> 01:26:19,461
Well, the former president had said that climate change is a hoax.
前总统曾说气候变化是一个骗局。

1248
01:26:20,561 --> 01:26:22,822
And what we know is that it is very real.
而我们知道它是非常真实的。

1249
01:26:22,962 --> 01:26:43,026
You ask anyone who lives in a state who has experienced these extreme weather occurrences, who now is either being denied home insurance or is being jacked up, you ask anybody who has been the victim of what that means in terms of losing their home, having nowhere to go, we know that we can actually deal with this issue.
你问任何一个经历过这些极端天气事件的州的居民，   现在要么被拒绝房屋保险，要么保险费被抬高，   你问任何一个经历过失去家园、无处可去的受害者，我们知道我们实际上可以解决这个问题。

1250
01:26:43,046 --> 01:26:45,727
The young people of America care deeply about this issue.
美国的年轻人对此问题非常关注。

1251
01:26:46,207 --> 01:26:58,436
And I am proud that as vice president over the last four years, we have invested a trillion dollars in a clean energy economy while we have also increased domestic gas production to historic levels.
作为副总统，我为在过去四年里在清洁能源经济上投资了一万亿美元而感到自豪，同时我们也将国内天然气生产提高到历史水平。

1252
01:26:58,876 --> 01:27:03,920
We have created over 800,000 new manufacturing jobs while I have been vice president.
在我担任副总统期间，我们创造了超过80万个新的制造业岗位。

1253
01:27:04,300 --> 01:27:10,465
We have invested in clean energy to the point that we are opening up factories around the world.
我们在清洁能源方面的投资已经使我们在全球范围内开设了工厂。

1254
01:27:10,485 --> 01:27:13,046
Donald Trump said he was going to create manufacturing jobs.
唐纳德·特朗普曾说他会创造制造业岗位。

1255
01:27:13,307 --> 01:27:14,768
He lost manufacturing jobs.
他却失去了制造业岗位。

1256
01:27:15,248 --> 01:27:30,574
And I'm also proud to have the endorsement of the United Auto Workers and Sean Fain, who also know that part of building a clean energy economy includes investing in American-made products, American automobiles it includes.
我还为获得美国汽车工人联合会和肖恩·费因的支持而感到自豪，他们也知道，建设清洁能源经济的一部分包括投资于美国制造的产品，包括美国汽车。

1257
01:27:31,394 --> 01:27:38,984
growing what we can do around American manufacturing and opening up auto plants, not closing them like happened under Donald Trump.
扩大我们在美国制造业的能力，开设汽车工厂，而不是像唐纳德·特朗普执政时那样关闭它们。

1258
01:27:39,004 --> 01:27:40,525
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢您。

1259
01:27:40,545 --> 01:27:41,867
That didn't happen under Donald Trump.
这在唐纳德·特朗普执政期间并没有发生。

1260
01:27:41,887 --> 01:27:46,132
Let me just tell you, they lost 10,000 manufacturing jobs this last month.
让我告诉你，他们上个月失去了1万个制造业岗位。

1261
01:27:46,773 --> 01:27:48,494
It's going, they're all leaving.
它们在流失，所有的工作岗位都在消失。

1262
01:27:49,174 --> 01:27:54,255
They're building big auto plants in Mexico, in many cases owned by China.
他们在墨西哥建造大型汽车工厂，在许多情况下由中国拥有。

1263
01:27:54,555 --> 01:28:01,157
They're building these massive plants and they think they're going to sell their cars into the United States because of these people.
他们建造这些巨大的工厂，认为他们可以把汽车卖到美国，因为这些人。

1264
01:28:01,597 --> 01:28:05,739
What they have given to China is unbelievable, but we're not going to let that.
他们给中国的东西是不可思议的，但我们不会让这种情况继续。

1265
01:28:05,799 --> 01:28:10,200
We'll put tariffs on those cars so they can't come into our country because they will kill
我们会对那些汽车征收关税，以便它们无法进入我们的国家，因为它们会摧毁

1266
01:28:10,720 --> 01:28:22,468
the United Auto Workers and any auto worker, whether it's in Detroit or South Carolina or any other place, what they've done to business and manufacturing in this country is horrible.
美国汽车工人和任何汽车工人，无论是在底特律、南卡罗来纳州还是其他地方，他们对这个国家的商业和制造业所做的事情是可怕的。

1267
01:28:22,888 --> 01:28:25,550
We have nothing because they refuse.
我们一无所有，因为他们拒绝。

1268
01:28:25,790 --> 01:28:30,453
You know, Biden doesn't go after people because supposedly China paid him millions of dollars.
你知道，拜登并没有追究那些人，因为据说中国给了他数百万美元。

1269
01:28:30,493 --> 01:28:32,735
He's afraid to do it between him and his son.
他害怕在他和他的儿子之间做这件事。

1270
01:28:33,175 --> 01:28:35,077
They get all this money from Ukraine.
他们从乌克兰获得了所有这些资金。

1271
01:28:35,297 --> 01:28:37,899
They get all this money from all of these different countries.
他们从所有这些不同的国家获得了所有这些资金。

1272
01:28:38,220 --> 01:28:42,183
And then you wonder, why is he so loyal to this one, that one, Ukraine, China?
然后你会想，为什么他对这个、那个、乌克兰、中国如此忠诚？

1273
01:28:42,603 --> 01:28:43,084
Why is he?
为什么会这样？

1274
01:28:43,304 --> 01:28:47,508
Why did he get $3.5 million from the mayor of Moscow's wife?
他为什么会从莫斯科市长的妻子那里获得350万美元？

1275
01:28:47,868 --> 01:28:51,611
Why did he get — why did she pay him $3.5 million?
她为什么给他350万美元？

1276
01:28:52,232 --> 01:28:57,096
This is a crooked administration, and they're selling our country down the tubes.
这是一个腐败的政府，他们正在将我们的国家出卖。

1277
01:28:57,196 --> 01:28:58,277
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢您。

1278
01:28:58,537 --> 01:28:58,838
Thank you.
谢谢。

1279
01:28:59,198 --> 01:29:05,543
We'll be right back with closing statements from both of our candidates, an historic night, this ABC News presidential debate from Philadelphia.
我们将很快回来，听取两位候选人的总结发言，今晚的ABC新闻总统辩论将是历史性的，来自费城。

1280
01:29:05,603 --> 01:29:12,988
Back in a moment.
马上回来。

1281
01:29:13,008 --> 01:29:17,011
The ABC News presidential debate will continue after this.
ABC新闻总统辩论将在此之后继续。

1282
01:29:18,613 --> 01:29:26,659
Live from the National Constitution Center in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, here again, David Muir and Lindsay Davis.
从宾夕法尼亚州费城的国家宪法中心现场直播，再次欢迎大卫·穆尔和林赛·戴维斯。

1283
01:29:27,571 --> 01:29:28,391
Welcome back tonight.
欢迎回来。

1284
01:29:28,431 --> 01:29:30,052
The time has come for closing statements.
现在是总结发言的时间。

1285
01:29:30,112 --> 01:29:31,853
And Vice President Harris, we begin with you.
哈里斯副总统，我们从您开始。

1286
01:29:33,813 --> 01:29:46,378
So I think you've heard tonight two very different visions for our country, one that is focused on the future and the other that is focused on the past and an attempt to take us backward.
今晚你们听到了两种截然不同的国家愿景，一种关注未来，一种则试图让我们回到过去。

1287
01:29:48,032 --> 01:29:49,132
But we're not going back.
但我们不会退回去。

1288
01:29:49,933 --> 01:29:55,595
And I do believe that the American people know we all have so much more in common than what separates us.
我相信美国人民知道，我们之间有许多共同点，而非分歧。

1289
01:29:56,035 --> 01:29:58,736
And we can chart a new way forward.
我们可以开辟一条新的前进道路。

1290
01:29:59,536 --> 01:30:11,761
And a vision of that includes having a plan, understanding the aspirations, the dreams, the hopes, the ambition of the American people, which is why I intend to create
这个愿景包括制定计划，理解美国人民的愿望、梦想、希望和雄心，因此我打算创造

1291
01:30:12,341 --> 01:30:27,021
an opportunity economy, investing in small businesses, in new families, in what we can do around protecting seniors, what we can do that is about giving hardworking folks a break and bringing down the cost of living.
一个机会经济，投资于小企业、新家庭，以及我们在保护老年人方面可以做的事情，给予辛勤工作的民众减负，降低生活成本。

1292
01:30:27,762 --> 01:30:45,266
I believe in what we can do together that is about sustaining America's standing in the world and ensuring that we have the respect that we so rightly deserve, including respecting our military and ensuring we have the most lethal fighting force in the world.
我相信我们可以共同努力，维持美国在世界上的地位，并确保我们获得应有的尊重，包括尊重我们的军队，确保我们拥有世界上最强大的战斗力量。

1293
01:30:45,906 --> 01:30:55,529
I will be a president that will protect our fundamental rights and freedoms, including the right of a woman to make decisions about her own body and not have her government tell her what to do.
我将成为一位保护我们基本权利和自由的总统，包括女性对自己身体做决定的权利，而不让政府告诉她该做什么。

1294
01:30:56,309 --> 01:30:59,150
I'll tell you, I started my career as a prosecutor.
我跟你说，我的职业生涯是作为检察官开始的。

1295
01:30:59,230 --> 01:31:03,731
I was a DA, I was an Attorney General, a United States Senator, and now Vice President.
我曾是地方检察官，担任过检察长、美国参议员，现在是副总统。

1296
01:31:03,791 --> 01:31:05,751
I've only had one client, the people.
我只服务过一个客户，那就是人民。

1297
01:31:06,471 --> 01:31:13,353
And I'll tell you, as a prosecutor, I never asked a victim or a witness, are you a Republican or a Democrat?
作为检察官，我从来没有问过受害者或证人，你是共和党人还是民主党人？

1298
01:31:14,033 --> 01:31:16,574
The only thing I ever asked them, are you okay?
我唯一问过他们的就是，你还好吗？

1299
01:31:17,970 --> 01:31:24,793
And that's the kind of president we need right now, someone who cares about you and is not putting themselves first.
这就是我们现在需要的那种总统，关心你的人，而不是把自己放在第一位。

1300
01:31:25,674 --> 01:31:38,480
I intend to be a president for all Americans and focus on what we can do over the next 10 and 20 years to build back up our country by investing right now in you, the American people.
我打算成为所有美国人的总统，专注于我们在未来10年和20年内可以做的事情，通过现在投资于你们，美国人民，重建我们的国家。

1301
01:31:39,000 --> 01:31:40,901
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢您。

1302
01:31:41,001 --> 01:31:41,662
President Trump?
特朗普总统？

1303
01:31:43,180 --> 01:31:48,364
So she just started by saying she's going to do this, she's going to do that, she's going to do all these wonderful things.
她刚才开始说她要做这个，她要做那个，她要做所有这些美好的事情。

1304
01:31:48,784 --> 01:31:50,505
Why hasn't she done it?
那她为什么没有做到呢？

1305
01:31:50,945 --> 01:31:53,047
She's been there for three and a half years.
她已经在那里三年半了。

1306
01:31:53,427 --> 01:31:56,149
They've had three and a half years to fix the border.
他们已经有三年半的时间来解决边境问题。

1307
01:31:56,549 --> 01:31:58,110
They've had three and a half years to
他们已经有三年半的时间来

1308
01:31:59,031 --> 01:32:01,373
create jobs, and all the things we talked about.
创造就业机会，以及我们讨论过的所有事情。

1309
01:32:01,774 --> 01:32:03,635
Why hasn't she done it?
那她为什么没有做到呢？

1310
01:32:04,056 --> 01:32:11,382
She should leave right now, go down to that beautiful White House, go to the Capitol, get everyone together and do the things you want to do.
她现在应该离开，去那座美丽的白宫，去国会，把大家聚在一起，做她想做的事情。

1311
01:32:11,402 --> 01:32:17,028
But you haven't done it, and you won't do it, because you believe in things that the American people don't believe in.
但你没有做到，而且你也不会做到，因为你相信的是美国人民不相信的事情。

1312
01:32:17,488 --> 01:32:19,350
You believe in things like
你相信的事情，比如说

1313
01:32:19,690 --> 01:32:20,511
We're not going to frack.
我们不会进行水力压裂。

1314
01:32:20,591 --> 01:32:21,912
We're not going to take fossil fuel.
我们不会使用化石燃料。

1315
01:32:21,932 --> 01:32:26,795
We're not going to do things that are going to make this country strong, whether you like it or not.
我们不会做那些会让这个国家强大的事情，无论你喜欢与否。

1316
01:32:27,275 --> 01:32:28,296
Germany tried that.
德国试过那样做。

1317
01:32:28,656 --> 01:32:33,440
And within one year, they were back to building normal energy plants.
在一年内，他们又开始建造常规能源厂。

1318
01:32:33,740 --> 01:32:34,701
We're not ready for it.
我们还没有准备好。

1319
01:32:35,021 --> 01:32:39,444
We can't sacrifice our country for the sake of bad vision.
我们不能为了糟糕的愿景牺牲我们的国家。

1320
01:32:39,744 --> 01:32:41,586
But I just ask one simple question.
但我只问一个简单的问题。

1321
01:32:42,106 --> 01:32:43,907
Why didn't she do it?
她为什么没有做到？

1322
01:32:44,208 --> 01:32:45,448
We're a failing nation.
我们是一个失败的国家。

1323
01:32:46,289 --> 01:32:48,930
We're a nation that's in serious decline.
我们是一个严重衰退的国家。

1324
01:32:49,230 --> 01:32:51,231
We're being laughed at all over the world.
我们在全世界都被嘲笑。

1325
01:32:51,411 --> 01:32:52,531
All over the world, they laugh.
全世界都在笑。

1326
01:32:52,631 --> 01:32:53,932
I know the leaders very well.
我非常了解这些领导人。

1327
01:32:53,972 --> 01:32:55,072
They're coming to see me.
他们来见我。

1328
01:32:55,392 --> 01:32:56,253
They call me.
他们给我打电话。

1329
01:32:56,673 --> 01:32:58,453
We're laughed at all over the world.
我们在全世界都被嘲笑。

1330
01:32:58,493 --> 01:33:00,854
They don't understand what happened to us as a nation.
他们不理解我们作为一个国家发生了什么。

1331
01:33:01,174 --> 01:33:02,175
We're not a leader.
我们不是领导者。

1332
01:33:02,515 --> 01:33:04,716
We don't have any idea what's going on.
我们不知道发生了什么。

1333
01:33:05,056 --> 01:33:07,197
We have wars going on in the Middle East.
我们在中东有战争。

1334
01:33:07,237 --> 01:33:10,898
We have wars going on with Russia and Ukraine.
我们与俄罗斯和乌克兰之间有战争。

1335
01:33:11,258 --> 01:33:17,805
We're going to end up in a third world war and it'll be a war like no other because of nuclear weapons, the power of weaponry.
我们将陷入第三次世界大战，这将是一场前所未有的战争，因为核武器和武器的力量。

1336
01:33:18,405 --> 01:33:21,088
I rebuilt our entire military.
我重建了我们的整个军队。

1337
01:33:21,528 --> 01:33:24,531
She gave a lot of it away to the Taliban.
她把很多武器交给了塔利班。

1338
01:33:25,132 --> 01:33:26,693
She gave it to Afghanistan.
她把它给了阿富汗。

1339
01:33:27,094 --> 01:33:32,459
What these people have done to our country and maybe toughest of all is allowing millions of
这些人对我们国家所做的事情，也许最糟糕的是允许数百万

1340
01:33:32,959 --> 01:33:34,720
people to come into our country.
人涌入我们的国家。

1341
01:33:34,820 --> 01:33:37,861
Many of them are criminals, and they're destroying our country.
他们当中许多人是罪犯，他们在摧毁我们的国家。

1342
01:33:38,241 --> 01:33:43,503
The worst president, the worst vice president in the history of our country.
历史上最糟糕的总统，最糟糕的副总统。

1343
01:33:43,843 --> 01:33:45,383
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢您。

1344
01:33:45,523 --> 01:33:51,485
And that is our ABC News presidential debate from here in Philadelphia at the National Constitution Center.
这就是我们在费城国家宪法中心的ABC新闻总统辩论。

1345
01:33:51,966 --> 01:33:52,706
I'm Lindsay Davis.
我是林赛·戴维斯。

1346
01:33:52,846 --> 01:33:53,646
And I'm David Muir.
我是大卫·穆尔。

1347
01:33:53,686 --> 01:33:55,087
Thank you for watching here in the U.S.
感谢您在美国和

1348
01:33:55,167 --> 01:33:57,848
and all over the world and from all of us here at ABC News.
全世界收看，来自我们ABC新闻的所有人。

1349
01:33:58,388 --> 01:33:58,668
Good night.
晚安。

1350
01:34:03,046 --> 01:34:03,868
Thanks for watching.
感谢观看。

1351
01:34:03,988 --> 01:34:10,720
